        "slug": "goal-plan-builder",
        "name": "Goal Plan Builder",
        "oneLiner": "A 60-second quiz matches GTA shoppers to one of six goal plans built from real Meal Butler meals, sold as a skip-anytime subscription (weekly, every 2 weeks or a monthly Freezer Fill) with 10% off.",
        "headline": "Standing orders turn one-off Meal Butler carts into predictable, recurring revenue at about 40% gross margin, using meals J&W already cooks.",
        "focus": "Quiz-led goal plans on a skip-anytime subscription",
        "mechanism": "J&W adds a quiz and six goal plans (Lean, Lean Bulk, Athlete, Protein & Greens, GLP-1 Companion, Busy Family) built only from current Meal Butler items. Examples: the Jerk Chicken pre-set at $12.99 (4oz); Chicken Breast Souvlaki 6oz at $6.93 with 6oz white basmati at $2.31 and broccoli at $1.39; 4oz salmon at $7.99; Egg White Bites at $5.25; Lemon Chicken Rice Soup at $8.99. Each box (10 to 40 meals) is priced as the sum of those real items, then 10% off on subscription. That lands at $7.30 a meal (GLP-1 Companion, 14 meals) to $13.02 (Lean Bulk), against about $16 to $27 for GTA goal plans. Customers choose weekly, every 2 weeks or a monthly Freezer Fill (possible only because J&W freezes its meals in vacuum packs), and can skip, swap or pause until Sunday night. If they change nothing, a Butcher's Pick box ships. A household box puts several people's plans in one delivery with one fee, and every box rides the existing Tue to Fri routes or free pickup at Brimley Rd.",
        "modelledOn": {
          "name": "Power Kitchen",
          "url": "https://powerkitchen.ca/",
          "scope": "GTA (East York, Toronto)",
          "short": "Quiz-matched goal meal plans on a skip-anytime subscription",
          "what": "Family-owned, bootstrapped GTA meal-prep company (46 Hollinger Rd, about 10 km from Brimley Rd). It sells eight goal plans (Power, Pro Athlete, GLP-1 Support, Low Carb, Clean Bulking, Keto, Lean Muscle, Vegan) through a plan-matching quiz. The subscription auto-renews and can be skipped, paused or edited before a hard cut-off. It also runs a sticky custom-meal builder, a one-month trial, a prepaid 6-week program, rewards, referrals and an ambassador program.",
          "proof": "Verified Oct 16 2026: goal boxes list at $16.22-$36.95 a meal (Power and Lean Muscle $17.85-$23.95; GLP-1 Support $21.76-$27.96). Subscribe discount 5% plus 5% credit. One-Month Trial $365-$535 for 20 meals. 4.7 stars from 564 Google reviews. 185 SKUs, all updated Oct 16 2026. Own fleet to about 40 cities on Sunday and Wednesday. Stack includes Klaviyo, Triple Whale and Sezzle. Revenue not published; estimate about C$3-7M a year (low confidence).",
          "jwEdge": "J&W is its own Ontario-inspected butcher (plant since 2008, family butchers since 1995). Recipes are salt and sugar free with no added oils. Plan meals cost $7.30-$13.02 with Subscribe & Save, roughly 25-45% less per like-for-like meal (est.). Frozen vacuum packs allow a monthly Freezer Fill and long-haul Ontario routes that fresh rivals cannot serve. A household box covers several people in one order, which Power Kitchen cannot do. Credits apply automatically. J&W also has bigger social proof: 4.8 stars from 611 Google reviews and 30K Instagram followers."
        },
        "year1": {
          "low": 171000,
          "mid": 341000,
          "high": 568000
        },
        "runRate": 726000,
        "marginPct": 40,
        "startMonth": 2,
        "mathYear1": "Subscribers ramp from 0 (Nov 2026 build month) to about 239 by Oct 2027. New subscribers: Dec 25, Jan 60, Feb 45, Mar 35, Apr 35, May 30, Jun 25, Jul 25, Aug 30, Sep 40, Oct 40 = 390, with 10% monthly churn. That gives 1,626 subscriber-months (avg 136 active) x $243.75 a month ($125 box after 10% off x 26 deliveries x 0.9 not skipped / 12) = $396K. Add 220 one-off plan boxes x $135 = $30K. Gross $426K x 0.8 incrementality = ~$341K added revenue (mid). Low: 245 new, 13% churn, $120 box, 12% skipped, 113 one-offs at $125, x0.75 = ~$171K. High: 555 new, 8% churn, $130 box, 325 one-offs at $140, x0.85 = ~$568K.",
        "mathRunRate": "Year 2 (Nov 2027-Oct 2028): start with ~239 active, add 35 a month, churn 9%. Average ~299 active x $2,925 a year ($125 x 26 x 0.9) = $875K, plus 240 one-off boxes x $135 = $32K. Gross $907K x 0.8 incrementality = ~$726K a year added revenue. Low ~$371K (25 adds a month, 12% churn); high ~$1.17M (45 adds a month, 8% churn; needs a second packing shift).",
        "mathNotes": [
          "Plan prices are sums of J&W's real Oct 16 2026 online prices. Example: Lean Bulk 10 meals = $144.65 one-off, $130.18 with 10% Subscribe & Save ($13.02 a meal).",
          "Revenue counts only subscribers who were not already weekly Meal Butler buyers. The 10% given to existing buyers who switch (~60 people, ~$13K in year 1) is counted as a cost, not as revenue.",
          "Gross margin 40% after the 10% discount (model-assumptions.md). Year 1 mid: $350K x 40% = $140K gross profit, minus ~$89K all-in JW costs = ~$51K contribution before Minastech's fee.",
          "Year 2: $757K x 40% = $303K gross profit, minus ~$120K running costs = ~$183K contribution.",
          "Cross-check: market-benchmarks.md section 11 says ~320 active every-2-weeks subscribers at $120 is about $1M gross. This play's year-2 average of 312 at $125 with 10% skips gives $914K gross.",
          "Volume: ~68 extra boxes a week (~850 meals) on average in year 1, ~146 a week (~1,800 meals) in year 2. Today J&W runs an estimated 60-160 delivery orders a week, so plant capacity must be confirmed.",
          "Delivery runs on existing routes. The customer pays the $20-$35 route fee, which covers an owned-route stop at $8-$14. No new route days.",
          "Year 1 is +14% on the ~$2.5M mid baseline; run-rate is +30%. Both are within the typical range for one play."
        ],
