        "prototype": {
          "concept": "Shows how J&W can sell the meals it already cooks as goal plans on a subscription, the way Power Kitchen does, but in J&W's voice and at J&W's prices. A shopper answers an 8-step quiz and gets a named plan with est. macros and a real price per meal, built from current Meal Butler SKUs. They subscribe weekly, every 2 weeks or as a monthly Freezer Fill, then manage it in a My Plan portal (skip, swap, pause, cancel with a save offer). The JW team view shows subscribers, the Monday prep sheet, route impact and AI-agent drafts waiting for approval.",
          "wow": "Pick a goal and a priced, macro-counted box of real J&W meals assembles itself as a stack of kraft freezer bags in the sticky bag. Flip 'Every 2 weeks' to 'Monthly Freezer Fill' and the stack grows to a month of meals, the price per meal holds, and 'Route fees a month' drops from 2 x $20 to 1 x $20.",
          "design": {
            "inspiredBy": "Power Kitchen's structure: thin cut-off announcement bar, quiz card with a step tracker and encouraging notes, goal-plan cards with macro chips and a plan accent colour, a sticky builder bag with a 'meals chosen' counter, and a dark rounded trust panel. Rebuilt in J&W's laurel navy, Meal Butler slate purple and sky blue on a warm kraft-cream ground with a premium serif, plus butcher-heritage cues (kraft paper, vacuum-pack freezer bags).",
