        "prototype": {
          "concept": "A partner-facing wholesale front door that J&W does not have today: who it serves, tiered Concept pricing on real J&W products, a shoppable partner catalogue with case packs, a co-branded label studio, and a two-minute application with an instant AI pre-check. A 'Partner portal (demo)' mode shows a signed-in gym approving an AI-drafted standing order, with invoices, member-code results and freezer status. The JW team view shows the applications queue, AI drafts to approve, partner accounts, production and route impact, and receivables. Every flow ends in the framework's demo checkout on J&W's real routes. File: site/prototypes/02-pro-partner-portal.html, JWC.init({ n: 2 }).",
          "wow": "Build your freezer: the visitor types a business name, picks a city and drags a 'meals a week' slider. A CSS glass-door freezer fills shelf by shelf with real J&W product photos, its header reads 'FUELLED BY J&W AT {NAME}', and a receipt shows the tier, what they pay ($577.06 at Pro for 48 meals), what members pay ($721.32), what they keep ($144.26 a week, about $7,213 a year) and their route day ('GTA 2 · Wednesday · order by Sunday'). One tap, 'Order this freezer fill', puts it in the cart.",
          "design": {
            "inspiredBy": "Icon Meals' wholesale page structure (proof, segments, plant story, shoppable grid with macros and steppers; white sticky header, full-bleed hero with dark overlay, alternating light canvas and dark bands, uppercase tracked headings), rebuilt in J&W laurel navy with butcher-shop warmth. Partner portal patterns borrow from B2B dashboards. No Icon text, logos or photos, and no fake partner-logo wall.",
