            {
              "name": "S11 FAQ",
              "purpose": "Answer the trade questions plainly.",
              "content": "Accordion. 'What's the minimum order?' 12 cooked meals or one butcher case. Standing orders of $150 or more drop free on your route day. / 'When do you deliver?' On our weekly routes: Tuesday Durham, Wednesday Toronto and Mississauga, Thursday Halton and Hamilton, Friday York and Peel. Order by Sunday for the next week. Pickup at Brimley Rd is always free. / 'How do I pay?' By card for your first four orders. After that, approved partners get net-15 invoices. / 'How does the freezer loan work?' Average $300 a week for eight weeks and we lend you a branded reach-in freezer with a temperature sensor. We own it and service it, and we take it back if you stop ordering. You supply the outlet. / 'How long does the food keep?' Everything is flash-frozen and vacuum-sealed, and each pack carries a best-before date. Keep it at −18°C or colder. / 'Can I sell online?' In person only. Your members can order from us online with your member code, and you earn credit. / 'Do labels show allergens and nutrition?' Every partner pack carries ingredients, allergens, net weight, best-before and our plant details. Nutrition facts are being added for partner products. / 'Can you deliver outside Ontario?' Not yet. Our plant is provincially inspected, so we sell within Ontario."
