        "cfo": {
          "changed": true,
          "reason": "Three fixes. (1) Year 1 counted 4.33 order weeks a month (52 a year), but year 2 counts 50 ordering weeks. Year 1 now uses 4.17. (2) The year-1 average order is $240, not $260. Most account-months come from accounts under six months old, and the play says new accounts start near $180. (3) Incrementality is 0.80, not 0.85. The play's own pitch says gyms and trainers 'already send people to J&W', so gym freezers partly replace direct orders (at 22% margin instead of 45%). They also sell to the same fitness buyers Plays 1 and 6 count. Year-1 contribution is now about -$26K ($39K gross profit against ~$65K costs, including $18K of freezers). Year 2 is about +$50K."
        }
