        "prototype": {
          "concept": "A clickable, mobile-first J&W Butcher Club page that does truLOCAL's best ideas (tier picker, points-budget box builder, free-for-life item, tap-to-explain comparison table, self-serve membership) the J&W way: real J&W cuts and prices, $/lb on every card, cut-to-thickness steaks, route-day delivery and Meal Butler cooked chicken as the free item. It adds beef and lamb shares with real cut sheets and deposits, plus a Wild Fork-town route finder. The JW team view shows a modelled week in April 2027: KPIs, the Monday pick list, route impact, agent drafts to approve, a retention queue, the share board and a monthly P&L.",
          "wow": "The box fills as you shop. A top-down freezer box fills with a tile for each pack (real J&W photo and name, sized by weight). A sky-blue points meter fills and a live line updates ('21.3 lb · about 68 servings · $11.22/lb'). The slate-purple free-for-life tile is pinned in a corner from the start. When points hit the budget, the lid closes with a navy laurel seal reading 'Packed at 2201 Brimley Rd' and the button changes to 'Join with this box'.",
          "design": {
            "inspiredBy": "truLOCAL's page structure (offer hero, value pillars, 3 steps, plan picker, points builder, tap-to-explain comparison table, social proof, story cards, closing CTA, floating order button), rebuilt with J&W's own identity: navy laurel, butcher-paper cream, oxblood buttons and heritage serif type. No truLOCAL green, copy, logos or photos.",
            "palette": [
              {
                "hex": "#154D8E",
                "role": "J&W laurel navy: brand, links, selected states"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#0F2E52",
                "role": "Deep navy: hero, comparison and closing bands"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#F6F0E4",
                "role": "Butcher-paper cream: page background"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#FFFFFF",
                "role": "Card white"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#1F2328",
                "role": "Charcoal ink: body text"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#8A2E2A",
                "role": "Oxblood: primary buttons and Club prices (white text, 8.4:1)"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#C8A15A",
                "role": "Brass: laurel ring, 'Free for life' ribbon, on dark backgrounds only"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#5B5A8C",
                "role": "Meal Butler slate purple: free cooked-chicken tile and cooked add-ons"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#7FB3D5",
                "role": "Meal Butler sky: frozen cues and points meter fill on dark"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#E2D8C4",
                "role": "Hairline borders and dividers"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#2E7D4F",
                "role": "Success ticks in the comparison table"
              }
            ],
            "displayFont": "Fraunces",
            "bodyFont": "Inter",
            "layout": "Mobile-first single column with 16 px gutters; desktop 12-column grid where the builder is a menu (8 cols) beside a sticky box panel (4 cols). Bands alternate cream and white, with two deep-navy bands (hero, price comparison) and a navy closing CTA. Card radius 14 px, pill buttons 48 px tall, Barlow Condensed 600 uppercase for badges, point chips and $/lb tags. Sticky bottom box bar on mobile once a box size is chosen.",
            "tone": "Plain, warm, proud family butcher speaking as 'we'. Short sentences, specific numbers, Canadian spelling, no hype. Every concept price is labelled Concept and every weight or serving count est."
          },
          "sections": [
            {
              "name": "Header",
              "purpose": "Brand and navigation",
