      {
        "n": 4,
        "slug": "jw-at-work",
        "name": "J&W at Work",
        "oneLiner": "A workplace meal perk for GTA employers: the company covers part or all of each Meal Butler meal, staff pre-order by Sunday, and J&W drops one order of named bags at the site on a route it already drives, with a loaned freezer for big shift sites.",
        "headline": "One dock drop of 50-plus prepaid meals on a route J&W already drives is the cheapest, highest-margin order J&W can take, and the employer subsidy keeps staff ordering every week.",
        "focus": "Employer-subsidised staff meals delivered on existing routes",
        "mechanism": "Employers choose a perk: $2 off up to the full price of each meal, 1-5 lunches covered a week, or everything up to a cap. The company's share is drawn from a prepaid wallet, so J&W carries no receivables. Staff join with their work email and order by J&W's existing Sunday cut-off from a 20-item At Work menu of real Meal Butler items, for example Teriyaki Chicken, Green Beans & Rice at $9.99, Jerk Chicken, Green Beans & Sweet Potato at $12.99, Egg White Bites at $5.25 and Steel Cut Oats at $4.40. Company-wide work pricing takes 5% off at 40+ items a week and 10% off at 100+ (a $12.99 meal becomes $11.69). Each week's orders go out as one stop of sealed, named bags on the route day that already serves that city, and delivery is free when the week tops $250. Sites with 75+ staff on site borrow a glass-door freezer that is restocked weekly and paid by QR code, and HR gets one split invoice, a monthly report and Team Table packs priced from published portions ($115.80-$147.88).",
        "modelledOn": {
          "name": "WeCook for Business",
          "url": "https://www.wecookmeals.ca/en/business",
          "scope": "Canada (Montreal)",
          "short": "Employer-subsidised ready meals, ordered by staff, delivered to the office",
          "what": "WeCook runs a workplace meal platform. The employer sets an allowance ($ per employee, $ per meal up to a cap, or N meals each) and invites staff, who must use the company email domain. Staff pick meals each week, and everything is rolled into one joint office order that cancels itself if nobody orders. The invoice splits what the company covered from what employees paid, and the price per meal falls with total company volume. Larger firms get on-site fridges.",
          "proof": "About 90,000 meals a week and nearly 400 staff (Retail Insider, Aug 2025). Trustpilot 4.8 from 6,584 reviews. The CEO puts the B2B meal at about $11.75, against $20-25 for traditional catering. Employers fund anywhere from $1 a meal to 100%, and the program fits companies of 20 to 500 employees. The dashboard copy was still live on Oct 16 2026.",
          "jwEdge": "J&W's frozen, vacuum-sealed meals suit an unattended office freezer, with no use-by waste. J&W's own Scarborough plant and its Tuesday-Friday routes already pass the Scarborough, Markham, North York, Vaughan and Mississauga business parks, while WeCook couriers from Quebec. Pre-set meals cost $9.99-13.99, at or below WeCook's $11.99-15.49, with macro-exact à la carte portions. J&W's promise is no added salt, sugar or oil; WeCook's sample bowl has 795-1,015 mg sodium. A butcher range (BBQ souvlaki cases) is something WeCook cannot offer."
        },
        "year1": {
          "low": 68000,
          "mid": 162000,
          "high": 323000
        },
        "runRate": 622000,
        "marginPct": 40,
        "startMonth": 3,
        "mathYear1": "Live from Jan 2027 (month 3). Team orders: accounts ramp 3 to 16 from Jan to Oct (3,4,6,8,10,11,12,12,14,16 = 96 account-months) x 4 order weeks x 40 items a week (new accounts start at about half the steady 55) x $10.00 average net item = $153,600. Freezers: 1 to 6 from Mar (30 freezer-months) x 4.2 weeks x $250 a week = $31,500. Team Table packs: 96 x 0.4 a month x $150 = $5,760. Gross $190,860 x 0.85 incrementality = $162K (mid). Low: 57 account-months x 4 x 30 items x $10 + 12 freezer-months x 4.2 x $200 + packs $1,710 = $80,190 x 0.85 = $68K. High: 145 account-months x 4 x 50 x $10.50 + 50 freezer-months x 4.2 x $300 + packs $11,963 = $379,463 x 0.85 = $323K.",
        "mathRunRate": "Year 2 (Nov 2027-Oct 2028): 22 average live accounts (16 rising to about 28) x 55 items a week x $10.00 x 48 weeks = $580,800, plus 9 freezers x $300 a week x 50 weeks = $135,000, plus 22 accounts x 5 packs x $150 = $16,500. Gross $732,300 x 0.85 incrementality = about $622K a year.",
        "mathNotes": [
          "Average net item price of $10.00: 75% lunches (average published 4 oz price of $12.32 across the 9 menu meals) and 25% breakfast items (about $5) give a $10.49 list mix, less about 5% for the volume tier.",
          "One steady account (100-140 staff on site, 25-30% ordering, 2.2 items each, 3 on-site days) is about 55 items and $550 a week, or about $26.4K a year, for roughly $10.6K gross profit at 40%.",
          "Gross profit at 40% is about $65K in year 1 and about $249K in year 2.",
          "JW's own costs are about $54.5K in year 1 ($13.8K setup, including 6 freezers, plus 11 × $3.7K a month), so year 1 is roughly break-even. Year 2 costs are about $80K, leaving about $170K contribution before Minastech's fee.",
          "Sanity check: year-1 mid is about 6.5% of JW's ~$2.5M mid-case revenue, and the run-rate is about 25%. Twenty-eight accounts by Oct 2028 is about 0.2% of the ~11-14K GTA sites with 50+ staff.",
          "Year-2 volume is about 1,470 extra items a week (about 1,210 pre-ordered plus about 260 from freezers), probably +1 cook/packer FTE. Plant headroom needs confirming.",
          "Incrementality is 0.85, the top of the shared 0.75-0.85 range, because employers are a new buyer. Some staff already buy J&W at home.",
          "Not counted here: gifts from the same employers (Play 5), resale by gyms and clinics (Play 2), fundraisers (Play 7), and staff who later subscribe at home (Plays 1 and 6)."
