        "prototype": {
          "concept": "An HR manager at a GTA employer designs a meal perk with live numbers, previews the staff app their team would use, tries the night-shift freezer, and then books a tasting or starts a 4-week pilot. Every product, price and route on the page is J&W's own; the work pricing, freezer loan and Team Table packs are labelled Concept. In JW team view, the same clicks appear as leads, pilots and orders. They sit beside a sample week of employer accounts, AI-drafted outreach and reminders waiting for approval, the cook-plan and route impact, and a company/staff split invoice. File: site/prototypes/04-jw-at-work.html. JWC.init({ n: 4, teamNote: 'The JW team sees every employer account, this week's team orders rolled into the cook plan and routes, and AI-drafted outreach, reminders and invoices waiting for approval.', chat: {...} }). Store keys: p4-leads, p4-pilots, p4-freezer, p4-approvals, p4-designer.",
          "wow": "The Perk Designer. HR drags the allowance slider, and a real meal card (Jerk Chicken, Green Beans & Sweet Potato, $12.99) splits live into a sky-blue 'Company covers $3.00' bar and a navy 'Staff pay $9.34' bar. Weekly lunches, monthly company cost and the pricing tier update as the slider moves, and a slate-purple badge animates when the team reaches Team or Site pricing ('Team pricing reached: 5% off for everyone'). One tap on 'See it in the staff app' carries the settings into the phone preview, which then reads 'Northline covers $3.00 off each meal'.",
          "design": {
            "inspiredBy": "WeCook for Business, ideas only: the lead form as the hero, an auto-scrolling benefit marquee, three numbered set-up cards, a 2x2 grid of objections, and round protein stickers on meal cards. Reworked with J&W's navy laurel, a frost-blue freezer motif and Meal Butler's slate purple, so it reads as crisp, premium and calm rather than WeCook green.",
            "palette": [
              {
                "hex": "#154D8E",
                "role": "Primary JW laurel navy: buttons, H1/H2, the 'Staff pay' bar"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#0F1E33",
                "role": "Ink: body text and dark bands"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#7FB3D5",
                "role": "Meal Butler sky: the 'Company covers' bar, highlights, focus rings (fill only, never text on white)"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#EAF3FA",
                "role": "Frost: freezer section and staff-app background"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#5B5A8C",
                "role": "Meal Butler slate purple: tier badges, HR report, Concept tags, team-view accents"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#F6F1E7",
                "role": "Oat: alternating section bands"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#E3A33B",
                "role": "Saffron: pilot-offer pill and low-stock badges (ink text on top)"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#2E7D6B",
                "role": "Teal: success ticks and confirmations"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#5A6472",
                "role": "Muted text"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#FFFFFF",
                "role": "Paper / cards"
              }
            ],
            "displayFont": "Bricolage Grotesque",
            "bodyFont": "Inter",
            "layout": "Mobile-first single column with a 16 px gutter and no horizontal scroll at 375 px. Desktop (1024 px and up):\n- Hero split 55/45, lead-form card on the right.\n- How it works in 3 columns.\n- Perk Designer: controls on the left, sticky result card on the right.\n- Staff app in a centred phone frame with callouts either side. Below 480 px the frame becomes a full-width card without device chrome.\n- Team Table packs in 3 columns; Fair questions in a 2x2 grid.\n\nStyling:\n- Cards: 16 px radius with a soft navy shadow.\n- Buttons: 10 px radius, at least 44 px tall.\n- All money figures use tabular numbers.\n- The marquee pauses on hover and focus, and shows as a static wrap under prefers-reduced-motion.\n- Bricolage Grotesque 600/700/800 for headings; Inter 400/500/600 for everything else.",
            "tone": "Neighbourly, plain and specific, like a family butcher talking to an office manager. Short sentences and Canadian spelling. No hype words (never 'unlock', 'seamless', 'revolutionize' or 'game-changer'), few em dashes. Every estimate says 'est.', and every Concept item says 'Concept'. Customer copy never names a competitor."
          },
          "sections": [
            {
              "name": "Sticky header",
              "purpose": "Brand the program and keep the main action one tap away.",
              "content": "Left: a navy laurel badge reading 'J&W', the wordmark 'J&W at Work', and a small sub-label 'from J&W Meal Butler'.\nNav: How it works · Menu · Freezer · Pricing · For HR. On mobile these become horizontal scroll chips.\nRight: a ghost button 'See the staff app' (scrolls to the phone) and a navy button 'Book a tasting' (scrolls to the hero form)."
            },
            {
              "name": "Hero with lead form",
              "purpose": "Say what it is in one breath and capture a sales-assisted lead above the fold, routing non-employer buyers to the right prototype.",
              "content": "Eyebrow: 'Workplace meals · Scarborough, since 1995'.\nH1: 'Lunch at work, cooked by your butcher.'\nSub: 'J&W at Work is a meal perk for GTA teams. You decide what the company covers. Your staff pick their meals by Sunday. We bring the whole order to one door on our regular route, packed and labelled by name.'\nSaffron pill: 'Pilot offer: a free tasting and 4 weeks of free delivery for our first 10 employers (Concept)'.\nProof chips: '4.8★ on Google · 611 reviews' · 'Ontario-inspected plant since 2008' · 'Frozen and sealed, so nothing spoils'.\n\nForm card 'Book a free team tasting'\n- Note: 'We bring 8 meals for your team to try, on our route day. Demo: nothing is sent.'\n- Fields:\n  - First name*, Last name*, Work email*, Company*, Phone.\n  - 'Who are the meals for?': Our employees (default) / Members or patients at a gym or clinic we run / A sports team or school group / Gifts for clients or staff / Just me.\n  - Staff on site: 20-49 / 50-99 / 100-249 / 250+.\n  - Site city: select from JWC.cities() plus Other.\n  - Notes: textarea, 200-character maximum, live counter 'x/200'.\n  - Checkbox: 'We already order from J&W'.\n- Live route hint once a city is chosen (built from JWC.routesFor), e.g. 'Good news: Markham is on our Friday route (GTA 4). Your team order would arrive Fridays.'\n- Routing notes instead of submitting:\n  - Gym or clinic: 'That's our Pro Partner Portal. See prototype 2 →'\n  - Team or school: 'See Team Fuel, prototype 7 →'\n  - Gifts: 'See the Corporate Gift Studio, prototype 5 →'\n  - Just me: 'See the Goal Plan Builder, prototype 1 →'\n- Button: 'Book my tasting'."
            },
            {
              "name": "Benefit marquee",
              "purpose": "Quick scannable reasons to care, borrowed as a format.",
              "content": "Auto-scrolling strip on oat background, navy text with small sky dots between items:\n- 'Less than a food-court lunch'\n- 'Frozen, so nothing goes to waste'\n- 'Protein printed on every meal'\n- 'One drop. One invoice.'\n- 'Skip a week, nothing ships'\n- 'Ontario chicken, no hormones or antibiotics'\n- 'A freezer on loan for 75+ staff'"
            },
            {
              "name": "How it works",
              "purpose": "Show the program is light work for HR.",
              "content": "H2: 'Set up in an afternoon. Runs itself after that.'\n\nThree numbered cards, each with a small UI or product image:\n1. 'Choose what the company covers.' 'Take $2 to $13 off each meal, cover a few lunches a week, or pay for all of it. Set a cap per person and a monthly budget, so there are no surprises.'\n2. 'Invite your team.' 'Staff join with their work email. Each week they pick meals by Sunday night. If they forget, a friendly reminder goes out on Thursday.'\n3. 'We bring it to one door.' 'Your order rides our regular Wednesday or Friday route. Each person's meals come in one sealed, named bag. One monthly invoice shows what the company paid and what staff paid.'\n\nFootnote: 'If nobody orders in a week, nothing ships and you pay nothing.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "Perk Designer (wow)",
              "purpose": "Let HR price a perk live, and see the company/staff split on a real J&W meal.",
              "content": "H2: 'Design your perk.' Sub: 'Move the sliders. The numbers change as you go. They are estimates to help you plan, not a quote.'\n\nControls\n- 'Staff on site': slider 20-500, default 100.\n- 'Days on site each week': segmented 1-5, default 3.\n- 'What the company covers', segmented:\n  - '$ off each meal': slider $0-12, step $0.50, default $3.\n  - 'Lunches covered': 1-5 per person per week, default 2.\n  - 'Everything': cap 1-5 a week, default 3.\n- 'Monthly budget cap (optional)': toggle plus $ input.\n\nResult card\n- Meal card: Jerk Chicken, Green Beans & Sweet Potato (JWC.img). Shows 'Published price $12.99', the work price at the current tier, and a split bar (sky 'Company covers $3.00' / navy 'Staff pay $9.34').\n- Rows, each marked est.:\n  - 'Staff likely to order each week (est.)'\n  - 'Lunches a week (est.)'\n  - Tier badge: Starter / Team, 5% off / Site, 10% off. On a tier change, animate 'Team pricing reached: 5% off for everyone'.\n  - 'Company cost per month (est.)'\n  - 'Staff pay per lunch, on average (est.)'\n- Line: 'Fully covered, a lunch here costs the company about $11.70, compared with $20 to $25 a head for typical office catering (est.)'.\n- If the budget cap is below the cost: 'Your cap covers about N weeks a month at this level. After that, staff still order at work prices.'\n\nButtons\n- 'Start a 4-week pilot with these settings' (opens onboarding).\n- 'See it in the staff app' (scrolls and updates the phone).\n- 'Email this summary to a colleague' (demo modal with a printable summary; 'Demo: nothing is sent').\n\nFormulas\n- avgLunch = 12.32\n- itemsPerPerson = 0.6 × days + 0.4\n- $ off X: p = min(0.60, 0.15 + 0.035 × X); lunches = round(N × p × itemsPerPerson); companyWeek = lunches × min(X, workPrice).\n- Lunches covered K: p = min(0.65, 0.35 + 0.06 × K); lunches = round(N × p × max(itemsPerPerson, K)); companyWeek = N × p × K × workPrice.\n- Everything, cap C: p = 0.60; lunches = round(N × p × min(C, days)); companyWeek = lunches × workPrice.\n- Tier: under 40 lunches 0%; 40-99 5%; 100+ 10%. workPrice = avgLunch × (1 − tier).\n- monthly = companyWeek × 4.33, capped by the budget if one is set.\n- staffPerLunch = workPrice − companyWeek / lunches.\n\nDefault check: 100 staff, 3 days, $3 off → p 25.5%, 56 lunches, Team tier, about $168 a week, about $727 a month, staff pay about $8.70 on average."
            },
            {
              "name": "Staff app preview",
              "purpose": "Show employees' side: domain-locked join, allowance applied before pay, named-bag drop.",
              "content": "H2: 'What your team sees.' Sub: 'A short weekly menu on their phone. Their allowance comes off before they pay.' Note: 'Sample company: Northline Logistics, Markham (fictional)'.\n\nPhone frame with 4 screens.\n\nA. Join\n- Title 'Join J&W at Work'. Text: 'Use your work email to join your company's meal perk.'\n- Email field and 'Send my sign-in link' button.\n- Hint chip: 'Try priya@northline.example'.\n- Any other domain shows: 'That email isn't on Northline's list. Use your @northline.example address, or ask HR to add you.'\n\nB. Menu\n- Header: 'Hi Priya' and 'Northline covers $3.00 off each meal, up to 5 a week'. The amount follows the Perk Designer.\n- Line: 'Order by Sunday, Oct 18 at midnight · Arrives Friday, Oct 23 at the shipping office'.\n- Tabs: Lunch / Breakfast / Wraps & soups.\n- Each card: photo, name, round navy sticker 'est. 38 g protein' (from JWC.macros), published price struck through next to the work price (Team tier), bold 'You pay $X', and +/- steppers.\n- Allowance meter: '3 of 5 covered this week'.\n\nC. Review\n- Rows, for example 4 meals (Jerk, Teriyaki, Salmon, Turkey) at work price $46.51; 'Northline covers −$12.00'; 'You pay $34.51'.\n- Pay with 'Card on file · DEMO •••• 4242' or 'Payroll deduction (if your company allows it)'.\n- Toggle: 'Repeat this order every week (skip any time)'.\n- Button: 'Confirm my meals'.\n\nD. Done\n- 'You're in Friday's Northline drop.'\n- 'Your bag will say PRIYA S. and sits on shelf 2 of the staff freezer.'\n- 'Thaw tomorrow's lunch in the fridge overnight, then heat 60 to 90 seconds.'\n- Buttons: 'Done' · 'Edit until Sunday'."
            },
            {
              "name": "The At Work Freezer",
              "purpose": "Sell the loaned-freezer idea for shift sites and let visitors try a 2 am purchase.",
              "content": "H2: 'The At Work Freezer.' Sub: 'For sites with 75 or more people on site, we lend you a glass-door freezer and keep it stocked. Good for night shifts, early starts and the days someone forgot to order.'\n\nBullets\n- 'Free loan. We deliver it, plug it in and restock it on your route day.'\n- 'Staff scan the QR code, pick a meal and pay with their allowance or a card.'\n- 'We count stock at every visit. If unpaid items go over 3% of what we stocked, the company covers the difference at work prices.'\n- 'Frozen meals keep for months, so nothing is thrown out on Friday.'\n\nInteractive: 'Try it: 2:10 am, night shift at a Scarborough care residence (sample).'\n- A CSS glass-door freezer with frost background and 3 shelves. Thumbnails with stock counts: Jerk Chicken ×6, Turkey, Spinach & Rice ×4, Salmon, Brussels & Quinoa ×3, Chicken Chili ×5, Egg White Bites ×8, Steel Cut Oats ×7.\n- Tap an item and a bottom sheet opens with a mock QR. Options: 'Use my allowance ($3.00 off)' / 'Pay the work price by card (demo)'. Then 'Pay $9.34'.\n- Confirmation: 'Paid. Enjoy your meal. 5 Jerk Chicken left.'\n- At 2 or fewer of an item, a saffron badge shows 'Low: restock Wednesday'.\n\nSmall print: 'The site provides a standard outlet. The freezer loan terms are a Concept for discussion.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "Team Table packs",
              "purpose": "Meeting and event add-ons built from real portions, including a butcher-only BBQ pack.",
              "content": "H2: 'Feeding a meeting? Order a Team Table pack.' Sub: 'For lunch-and-learns, all-hands and the summer BBQ. Packs ride the same route as your team order.'\n\nThree cards, each tagged Concept.\n\n1. 'Lunch & Learn Pack, 12 people', $147.88\n- Contents: '4 Souvlaki, Broccoli & Greek Potatoes · 4 Teriyaki Chicken, Green Beans & Rice · 4 Salmon, Brussels & Quinoa. Name labels and a printed menu card.'\n- Mix editor: steppers that must total 12, choosing from 6 favourite lunches. The price recalculates from published 4 oz prices.\n\n2. 'Breakfast Meeting Pack, 12 people', $115.80\n- Contents: '12 Egg White Bites, Spinach & Feta · 12 Steel Cut Oats.'\n\n3. 'Team BBQ Pack, about 25 people', $134.95\n- Contents: 'No-Salt Chicken Souvlaki Case (5 kg, about 50 skewers) · Tzatziki 1.5 L · 5 packs of Whole Grain Greek Pita. Raw skewers for your grill. Cook chicken to 74°C.'\n\nEach card has two buttons:\n- 'Add to cart' (JWC.cart.add).\n- 'Order this pack': JWC.checkout({title:'Team Table order', city:'Markham', extraRows:[{label:'At Work delivery credit (team order over $250)', amount:-20}], note:'Rides with the Northline team order on Friday'})."
            },
            {
              "name": "For HR",
              "purpose": "Show the monthly report and wellness add-ons that keep HR renewing.",
              "content": "H2: 'A monthly report you can send upstairs.'\n\nSample report card in slate purple, 'Northline Logistics · October 2026 (sample)':\n- 'Meals delivered: 470 (352 pre-ordered, 118 from the freezer)'\n- 'On-site staff who ordered each week: 31%'\n- 'Company covered: $1,410.00 · Staff paid: $3,434.88'\n- 'Average protein per lunch: 36 g (est.)'\n- 'Most ordered: Jerk Chicken, Green Beans & Sweet Potato'\n- 'Freezer shrink: 1.2%'\n\nLine: 'Each person's company-paid total is listed for payroll. Ask your payroll provider how to treat it.'\n\nAdd-ons:\n- 'Quarterly lunch-and-learn: 30 minutes with our team on protein, portions and meal prep. Free for accounts ordering 40+ items a week.'\n- 'Step-challenge prize: a $60 Meal Butler credit for your winner each quarter (Concept).'"
            },
            {
              "name": "Fair questions",
              "purpose": "Handle the four common objections (format idea from WeCook's myth-busters).",
              "content": "H2: 'Fair questions.' Four cards in a 2x2 grid:\n1. 'We don't have a kitchen.' → 'You need a microwave and some freezer space. Meals heat in 60 to 90 seconds once thawed. Sites with 75+ staff can borrow our freezer.'\n2. 'Half the team is remote on Fridays.' → 'Meals are frozen, so they keep. Staff can take theirs home, and anyone can skip a week. No orders means no delivery and no bill.'\n3. 'Healthy lunches are boring.' → 'Jerk chicken, Korean BBQ flank, Greek lemon souvlaki, teriyaki, honey garlic salmon. Our own marinades, cooked in our own plant.'\n4. 'HR doesn't need another job.' → 'Staff order for themselves. You get one invoice and one short report a month. Reminders and order roll-ups are handled for you.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "Who it's for and route check",
              "purpose": "Name the target segments and prove the site is on an existing route.",
              "content": "H2: 'Built for GTA workplaces on our routes.'\n\nFour tiles:\n- 'Hospitals, clinics and care homes': 'Night shifts and closed cafeterias. The freezer does the work.'\n- 'Warehouses, plants and distribution centres': 'No food court nearby, early starts, big shifts.'\n- 'Offices and studios': 'Hybrid teams on site two or three days a week. A lunch that brings people in.'\n- 'Property managers': 'A tenant amenity for your towers. Tenants order, you choose the perk.'\n\nRoute lookup: label 'Is your site on our route?'. An input using JWC.findCity / JWC.routesFor returns, for example, 'Vaughan: Friday route (GTA 4)'.\n\nRoute list:\n- Tue: Durham\n- Wed: Toronto, Scarborough, North York, East York, Etobicoke, Mississauga\n- Thu: Oakville, Burlington, Hamilton, Milton\n- Fri: Markham, Vaughan, Richmond Hill, Brampton, Newmarket, Aurora"
            },
            {
              "name": "Pricing",
              "purpose": "Plain work-pricing tiers and terms (Concept).",
              "content": "H2: 'Simple work pricing.' Tag: Concept.\n\nTable columns: Your company's weekly order | Price for everyone | Included.\n- 'Under 40 items' | 'Our published prices' | 'Free tasting, monthly report'\n- '40 to 99 items' | '5% off every item' | '+ quarterly lunch-and-learn'\n- '100 or more' | '10% off every item' | '+ a say in next month's menu'\n\nNotes:\n- 'Free delivery to one door on any week over $250. Under $250, the regular $20 route fee applies.'\n- 'At Work Freezer on loan for sites with 75+ staff on site and $250+ a week in combined orders.'\n- 'Your allowance comes off after the work price.'\n- 'No contract. Pilots run 4 weeks. After that, 30 days' notice.'\n- 'Prices in CAD. For your own staff, not for resale.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "Closing call to action",
