              "content": "Cards, each with Approve / Edit / Skip buttons. State is saved in p4-approvals.\n\n1. B2B prospecting and account agent: intro email to Maple Ridge Packaging (Markham, about 180 staff, Friday route).\n- Subject: 'Lunch for your night shift, from a Scarborough butcher'.\n- Body: 'Hi there, we're J&W Foods, a family butcher and meal-prep kitchen on Brimley Rd since 1995. Our truck is in Markham every Friday. We run a simple meal perk: you choose what the company covers, staff order by Sunday, and we drop everything at your door. Could we bring 8 meals for your team to try on Friday, Oct 30? Lucas, J&W Foods, (416) 298-1350. Reply STOP to opt out.'\n- Chip: 'CASL check: published business contact, relevant to role, unsubscribe included: OK'.\n\n2. At Work order desk agent: Thursday reminder SMS to 97 opted-in Northline staff who haven't ordered.\n- Text: 'Hi from J&W at Work. Your $3 lunch credit is waiting. Pick next week's meals by Sunday at midnight: [link]'.\n\n3. B2B prospecting and account agent (account health): 'Don Mills Design Co.: participation fell from 44% to 29% in 3 weeks. Suggest a free Breakfast Meeting Pack ($115.80 retail, about $64 food cost) for their Oct 28 all-hands, plus 2 new menu items.'\n\n4. Production forecast and prep-sheet agent: 'Add At Work volume to Monday's cook plan: +212 chicken breast portions (about 24 kg cooked, 32 kg raw at an est. 75% yield), +64 salmon, +58 tilapia, +120 egg-bite 2-packs, +60 oats.'\n\n5. Production forecast and prep-sheet agent: 'Freezer B (Milliken) sold out of Jerk Chicken by Tuesday two weeks running. Raise par from 8 to 14; cut Lemon Chicken Rice Soup from 8 to 4.'\n\n6. Route and delivery experience agent: 'Wednesday GTA 2: insert 7 At Work drops between stops 9 and 21. Adds about 52 min and 14 km. Text site contacts a 10:30 to 11:30 window.'\n\nPilots created in flow 2 add a card from the At Work order desk agent: 'Staff invite email for [company], ready to send Monday'."
