          "short": "US family butcher's B2B arm: certificates, volume programs, rewards tiers",
          "what": "A dedicated business-gifting program from a family butcher founded in 1917. It offers curated gift boxes (US$81 to $212) and 'Choice' certificates, where each recipient picks from a curated level and redeems online, by phone or by mail. Qualifying programs get logo and message branding. Multi-recipient orders go on one order form with a single invoice. It also offers pay-on-redemption for large programs, a month-by-month holiday planning calendar, and Business Rewards tiers by annual spend.",
          "proof": "Company claims of 5,000+ business clients, 350,000+ custom gift certificates and 700,000+ coolers to business recipients since 2020 (Omaha Steaks internal data, 2025; verified on the live page Oct 16, 2026). The 2026 holiday business guide runs US$100 to $180. Lead-form spend buckets run from under $100 to over $250. Business Rewards tiers sit at US$5K / $20K / $50K a year.",
          "jwEdge": "Omaha does not ship to Canada. J&W already delivers across the GTA and Ontario on its own weekly routes for $20 to $35, with free pickup in Scarborough. It cuts in its own Ontario-inspected plant and has a Greek-Canadian family story going back to the 1960s. It can also gift clean cooked Meal Butler meals, a wellness gift Omaha cannot offer. Omaha's B2B ordering still runs on an emailed Excel form. J&W's studio is self-serve and sorts the recipient list onto route days live."
