        "prototype": {
          "concept": "A premium, self-serve corporate gifting page for J&W. A buyer gets a price in two taps, picks a level and a real J&W box, and adds a logo and message with a live card preview. They upload a recipient list that sorts itself onto J&W's real route days, flags anyone outside Ontario, and turns missing addresses into Pick-a-Box certificates. They pay by demo card through JWC.checkout or request an invoice, and can see the page each recipient uses to redeem. The JW team view shows the Gift Desk pipeline, AI-drafted quotes, list checks and messages waiting for approval, a certificate ledger, and the December cut list and route impact.",
          "wow": "The buyer taps 'Use our sample list (25 people)', and the list visibly sorts itself into route-day groups: Tue Durham 4, Wed Toronto/Mississauga 7, Wed long 1, Thu Halton/Hamilton 3, Fri York/Peel 6, Fri long 1. Calgary and Montreal are flagged in terracotta ('We can only sell meat in Ontario. Removed, you won't be charged.') and the one person with no address becomes a Pick-a-Box certificate. Meanwhile the branded card preview shows the buyer's logo and message, and the sticky bar total updates to $3,351.50.",
          "design": {
            "inspiredBy": "Omaha Steaks Business Gifts: a dark full-bleed photo hero with a left headline, one pill CTA and an 'at a glance' card; a thin promo strip; a big-number proof band; three program cards; tier cards; numbered steps; a box builder with a sticky footer (points, price, Continue); an FAQ accordion; an inline lead form; a sticky action row. Burgundy is swapped for J&W laurel navy, with Mediterranean olive and terracotta, and the American heritage story becomes the J&W family story.",
