            "displayFont": "Fraunces",
            "bodyFont": "Inter",
            "layout": "Mobile-first single column at 375px with 16px gutters, scaling to a desktop max width of 1200px. The hero splits 7/5 with the 'Corporate gifts at a glance' card on the right; on mobile the card stacks under the headline. The proof band is 4 columns on desktop and 2x2 on mobile, with Fraunces numerals. Tier cards sit in a 4-across row on desktop and a horizontal snap scroller on mobile with the next card visible. The studio is a 4-step card with a progress bar and a sticky bottom bar (gifts, box, total, Continue) that only shows while the studio is in view. The redemption demo sits in a phone frame. The FAQ is an accordion. A sticky mobile action row (Call, Start, Pricing, Ask) has 44px+ targets. Section h2s are centred between hairline rules.",
            "tone": "Warm, plain and confident, like a family butcher who has done this for decades. Short sentences, Canadian spelling, real prices and real dates, no hype words. Quantified like Omaha, but the proof is J&W's own: since the 1960s, 1995, 2008, 4.8 stars."
          },
          "sections": [
            {
              "name": "Holiday strip",
              "purpose": "Create honest urgency with the real Holiday 2026 deadlines",
              "content": "Terracotta strip, white text: 'Holiday 2026: order by Sunday, Dec 6 for logo cards and delivery the week of Dec 14. Pick-a-Box certificates can go out by email until Dec 24.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "Hero",
              "purpose": "Say what it is and who it is for, with one clear CTA",
              "content": "Background: Gentleman's Box photo (JWC.img) under a midnight gradient. Eyebrow: 'J&W Corporate Gift Studio'. H1: 'Gifts your people will actually cook.' Sub: 'Ontario meat and clean Meal Butler meals, cut and packed by our family in Scarborough. Your logo on the card. We deliver on our own routes, or each person picks their own box with a J&W Pick-a-Box certificate.' Primary pill CTA: 'Start a gift order' (scrolls to the studio). Secondary link: 'Get your price in two taps'. 'Corporate gifts at a glance' card rows: 'From $84.99 a gift' / 'Volume pricing from 10 gifts' / 'Your logo and message, free' / 'Office drop, home delivery or Pick-a-Box certificate' / 'Pay by card, or by invoice for approved businesses' / 'Ontario recipients (our plant is provincially inspected)'."
            },
            {
              "name": "Your price in two taps",
              "purpose": "Omaha's two-tap lead qualifier, but it returns a real price at once",
              "content": "H2 'Your price in two taps'. Q1 'How many gifts?' pills: Under 10 / 10-49 / 50-99 / 100-249 / 250+ (midpoints 5/25/60/150/300; discount 0/5/8/10/12%). Q2 'About how much per gift?' pills: $90 / $130 / $200 / $350 (anchors: Ultimate BBQ Dad Pack $84.99, Gentleman's Box $129.99, Long Weekend Box $199, J&W Reserve Box $349 Concept). Result line, e.g. 'About $123.49 a gift after 5% volume pricing. 25 gifts = about $3,087.' Buttons: 'Build this order' (preloads the studio) and 'Send to our Gift Desk' (prefills the form). For 250+: 'Big programs can pay only for the certificates people redeem. Let's talk.' Small print: 'Volume pricing is a concept. Delivery is extra.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "Proof band",
              "purpose": "Heritage and trust using J&W's own facts",
