        "prototype": {
          "concept": "A mobile-first page where a shopper answers seven quick questions, sees their daily macros with the maths shown, and gets a Monday-to-Friday week of real Meal Butler portions they can swap, then buys it à la carte or as a Personal Macro Plan. It shows Calo's best idea, cooking to your own numbers, done by a Scarborough butcher with a personal label, an InBody scan at the store and a person behind the AI. The JW team view shows the coach desk: approvals of AI drafts, safety escalations, the client roster and the Saturday weigh-and-pack sheet on the existing route days.",
          "wow": "Type your name and press 'Print my label': a thermal-style J&W label slides out line by line with your name, the day, each component in grams and that meal's macros, built from the week the coach just made for you (e.g. 'FOR MARIA S. · TUESDAY · LUNCH / Greek Lemon Chicken Breast 180 g / Greek Lemon Potatoes 200 g / Green Beans 110 g / 519 kcal · P 63 g · C 51 g · F 7 g (est.) / Weighed 180 g · target 180 g ✓').",
          "design": {
            "inspiredBy": "Calo's split hero with a rotating audience line, macro-dot dish cards, the plan configurator's sticky live summary, the condensed kinetic statement band and the FAQ beside a 'talk to us' card. Rebuilt in J&W navy and Meal Butler slate purple with a butcher-paper label motif instead of Calo's green.",
            "palette": [
              {
                "hex": "#154D8E",
                "role": "J&W navy: primary buttons, links, logo, active tabs"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#0E2238",
                "role": "Night navy: kinetic band, Instagram phone frame, footer CTA, team headers"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#5B5A8C",
                "role": "Meal Butler slate purple: coach avatar, chat bubbles, protein dot, 'Most personal' badge"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#7FB3D5",
                "role": "Sky blue: fat dot, chips on dark, focus ring on dark"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#EAF1F8",
                "role": "Sky mist: alternate sections and intake card background"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#F6F1E6",
                "role": "Butcher paper: personal label and persona cards"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#D9982E",
                "role": "Harvest amber: carbs dot and bars only, never text"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#1D2433",
                "role": "Ink: headings and body text"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#5A6377",
                "role": "Slate: secondary text"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#2E7A57",
                "role": "Pine: 'On target' checks and success states"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#B4442F",
                "role": "Brick: escalation and medical flags in team view"
              }
            ],
            "displayFont": "Bricolage Grotesque",
            "bodyFont": "Inter",
            "layout": "Single column at 375px with 16px gutters, max width 1180px. Sticky 64px header. Hero two columns on desktop (text 6/11, visual 5/11), H1 40px mobile / 64px desktop, weight 800, tight leading. Planner 8/4 grid with a sticky summary on desktop; on mobile the summary is a bottom sheet that sits above the framework's cart and chat buttons. Cards 20px radius, panels 28px, pill buttons, soft navy shadows, 8px macro dots, 10px stacked macro bars. Label and macro numbers in IBM Plex Mono (Google Fonts URL: https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wdth,wght@12..96,75..100,400..800&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap). Kinetic band uses Bricolage Grotesque at width 75.",
            "tone": "Plain, warm, second person, short sentences, Canadian spelling, a little wit. Honest about estimates. Never 'revolutionize', 'unlock', 'seamless' or 'game-changer'."
          },
          "sections": [
            {
              "name": "Header",
              "purpose": "Brand and navigation",
              "content": "Logo ../assets/img/jw-logo.jpg (alt 'J&W Foods, Est. 1995'), wordmark 'Meal Butler' + chip 'AI Coach'. Anchors: How it works · Your numbers · Your week · Plans · Scans · FAQ. Button 'Start my plan'."
            },
            {
              "name": "Hero",
              "purpose": "Promise and two entry points",
              "content": "Eyebrow 'MEAL BUTLER AI COACH · CONCEPT'. H1 'Meals weighed to your macros, for' + rotating line 'early-shift nurses.' / 'Saturday lifters.' / 'people on a GLP-1.' / 'busy parents.' / 'marathon training.' (2.4 s, pause on hover, reduced motion shows 'for you.'). Sub: 'Tell the Butler your goal in two minutes. Get a week of J&W cooked portions sized to your numbers. Then our Scarborough kitchen weighs every portion to the gram and puts your name on the bag.' Buttons 'Start my plan' (scrolls to intake) and 'Chat with the Butler' (JWC.chat.open()). Trust line: '4.8★ from 611 Google reviews · No added salt, sugar or oil · Ontario-inspected kitchen since 2008'. Visual: real product photos (souvlaki, salmon, egg bites via JWC.img) with a floating label card 'FOR MARIA S. · MON · LUNCH / Chicken Breast Souvlaki 175 g / White Basmati Rice 200 g / Broccoli 110 g / 589 kcal · P 63 · C 63 · F 7 (est.)' and chip 'Protein today: 140 of 140 g'."
            },
            {
              "name": "How it works",
              "purpose": "Explain the three steps",
              "content": "H2 'Three steps. About two minutes.' 1 'Talk to the Butler': 'Answer seven quick questions here, or DM PLAN to @jwfoods on Instagram.' 2 'Get your week': 'The coach builds Monday to Friday from Meal Butler portions we already cook. Swap anything and watch the macros and price change.' 3 'Weighed, labelled, delivered': 'Buy it in our standard 4oz and 6oz sizes, or join the Personal Macro Plan and we weigh each portion to your grams, with your name on the bag.' Numbered badges in navy."
            },
            {
              "name": "Your numbers (intake)",
              "purpose": "Calo-style custom-macro stepper done as a chat",
              "content": "H2 \"Let's get your numbers\". Sub 'Seven questions. Demo: your answers stay on this device.' Chat-style stepper with coach avatar and progress dots. Q1 \"What's the goal?\" chips: Lose fat · Build muscle · Maintain and perform · Eat well on a GLP-1 medication. Q2 'A bit about you': age; sex ('used only for the calorie formula'); height cm or ft/in; weight kg or lb. Q3 'How many days a week do you train?' 0–7. Q4 'Which meals should we cover?' Lunch and dinner, Mon–Fri · Breakfast, lunch and dinner, Mon–Fri. Q5 'Anything you skip?' Fish · Beef · Spicy · Eggs · Dairy · Rice · Nothing. Q6 'Weekly food budget?' slider $100–$250, default $175, \"We'll tell you if your week goes over.\" Q7 'Where do you live?' JWC.cities() + 'Pick up at Brimley Rd', shows route day and fee. Safety check: 'Do any of these apply? Pregnant or breastfeeding · Diabetes · Kidney disease · A food allergy · Past eating disorder · Under 18.' Link 'Use demo answers' (Maria: lose fat, F, 38, 165 cm, 78 kg, 3 days, full day, no skips, $175, Scarborough). Result 'Your daily target (estimate)': 1,610 kcal · 140 g protein · 160 g carbs · 45 g fat, stacked bar (protein purple, carbs amber, fat sky), 'Edit macros' ±5 g steppers, expandable 'How we worked this out': 'Resting burn by the Mifflin-St Jeor formula: 1,460 kcal. Times 1.375 for 3 training days: 2,008 kcal. Minus 20% to lose fat: 1,610 kcal. Protein 1.8 g per kg. Fat 25% of calories. Carbs fill the rest. A registered dietitian reviews these rules (concept). General guidance, not medical advice.' Button 'Build my week'. If any safety box is ticked: card \"Let's get a person on this\" with 'Book a free 15-minute call'. Formula: BMR men 10·kg+6.25·cm−5·age+5, women −161; activity 0–1 days 1.2, 2–3 1.375, 4–5 1.55, 6–7 1.725; goal lose 0.80, maintain 1.00, build 1.10, GLP-1 0.75; protein g/kg lose 1.8, maintain 1.6, build 2.0, GLP-1 1.4 (cap 220 g); round kcal to 10, grams to 5."
            },
            {
              "name": "Your week (planner)",
              "purpose": "Bespoke week from real SKUs with swaps and live totals",
              "content": "H2 \"Here's your week, Maria.\" Sub 'Built from Meal Butler portions we cook every week. Tap Swap on anything.' Day tabs Mon–Fri; Breakfast / Lunch / Dinner cards with JWC.img photo, name, grams, macro dots, est. kcal, price, 'Swap'. Default week: Mon Chicken Breast Souvlaki 175 g / White Basmati 200 g / Broccoli 110 g + Salmon Fillet 230 g / Quinoa 200 g / Asparagus 110 g; Tue Greek Lemon Chicken 180 g / Greek Lemon Potatoes 200 g / Green Beans 110 g + Roasted Turkey Breast 180 g / Sweet Potato 200 g / Spinach 110 g; Wed Teriyaki Chicken 175 g / Cilantro Lime Rice 200 g / Broccoli & Cauliflower 110 g + Haddock Loin 255 g / Brown Basmati 200 g / Brussels Sprouts 110 g; Thu Korean BBQ Chicken 175 g / White Basmati 200 g / Green Beans 110 g + Beef Flank Steak 195 g / Baked Potato 200 g / Asparagus 110 g; Fri Arabic 7 Spice Chicken 160 g / Caribbean Rice & Beans 200 g / Mixed Veggies 110 g + Jerk Chicken 180 g / Sweet Potato 200 g / Green Beans 110 g; breakfast daily Egg White Bites, Spinach & Feta + Steel Cut Oats. Algorithm: Full Day breakfast fixed (290 kcal, P16, C31, F9.5 est.), lunch and dinner each get (daily − breakfast) ÷ 2; Lunch & Dinner plan gives each meal 35% of the day; veg 110 g (140 g GLP-1); carbs (meal carbs − veg carbs) ÷ carb per g clamped 60–200 g; protein (meal protein − carb and veg protein) ÷ protein per g clamped 85–255 g (GLP-1 cap 140 g); round to 5 g; macros from perOz ÷ 28.35; exact price = per-oz price of largest variant × grams ÷ 28.35; à la carte uses the nearest standard variant, qty 1. Day bar: calories and protein vs target, pine 'On target' when protein within ±10%, amber 'Light on calories' when >15% under with tip 'Add an Apple Cinnamon Oat Bar ($4.99)'. Note: 'We cook with no added oil, so fat runs low. Salmon twice a week helps.' Swap sheet: 4 same-role options respecting skips with deltas (e.g. 'Chicken Breast Souvlaki 175 g · −$1.47 · +4 g fat · same protein, est.') and 'Use this'. Sticky summary: 'Protein average 140 g a day (target 140)', 'À la carte, standard sizes: $159.12', 'Personal Macro Plan, Full Day · Plus: $189 a week, weighed to your grams'. Buttons 'Add this week to cart' and 'Make it my Personal Macro Plan'. Small text: \"Standard sizes are close to your grams, not exact. That's what the plan fixes.\" Budget flag with 'Budget swap' (Beef Flank Steak → Chicken Breast Souvlaki) if over budget. Link 'Want a standing order at 10% off? See Goal Plans (Prototype 1).'"
            },
            {
              "name": "Your name on every bag",
              "purpose": "The wow: personal label printing",
              "content": "H2 'Your name on every bag.' Sub \"Plan meals are cooked with everyone else's, then weighed to your grams and sealed with a label made for you.\" Input 'First name and last initial' (labelled). Day and meal pickers. Button 'Print my label' animates a thermal label sliding down line by line in IBM Plex Mono on butcher paper: 'J&W MEAL BUTLER · PERSONAL MACRO PLAN / FOR MARIA S. / TUESDAY · LUNCH / Greek Lemon Chicken Breast 180 g / Greek Lemon Potatoes 200 g / Green Beans 110 g / 519 kcal · P 63 g · C 51 g · F 7 g (est.) / Weighed 180 g · target 180 g ✓ / Packed at 2201 Brimley Rd, Scarborough / Keep frozen. Thaw overnight, reheat 60–90 s.' plus a CSS barcode stripe. Caption 'Macros are estimates from our recipes and Health Canada nutrient data.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "Plans",
              "purpose": "À la carte vs Personal Macro Plan with Concept pricing",
              "content": "H2 'Two ways to eat your plan.' Card A 'À la carte · Free coach, standard sizes': 'Pay per item, as always' · 'Free AI coach on the site and Instagram' · '3oz, 4oz and 6oz portions' · 'Free pickup, or $100 minimum on routes' · 'Order by Sunday for next week'; button 'Add my week to cart'. Card B, badge 'Most personal', 'Personal Macro Plan (Concept)': toggles Lunch & Dinner / Full Day and Regular / Plus / Performance (auto-picked: Regular up to 120 g protein a day, Plus 121–160 g, Performance over 160 g): Lunch & Dinner $119 / $139 / $159, Full Day $169 / $189 / $219 a week. Bullets: 'Every portion weighed to your grams' · 'Your name, day and macros on each meal' · 'Weekly check-in: the AI drafts it, a person at J&W approves it' · 'InBody scan at Brimley Rd every 4 weeks, included' · 'Free 15-minute call with a registered dietitian to start' · 'Skip or pause before the Sunday cut-off. No contract.' Button 'Start my Personal Macro Plan'. Footnote: \"Concept pricing built from J&W's own per-ounce prices. Your week at exact grams is about $187 à la carte. GTA premium meal prep runs $14 to $30 a meal.\""
            },
            {
              "name": "Kinetic band",
              "purpose": "Memorable statement",
              "content": "Marquee on night navy in Bricolage Grotesque width 75: 'WEIGHED. LABELLED. YOURS.' Smaller line: 'Cut, cooked and portioned in Scarborough since 1995.' Static under reduced motion."
            },
            {
              "name": "Scans",
              "purpose": "Store visit and re-plan loop",
              "content": "H2 'Check in every four weeks.' Sub 'Drop by 2201 Brimley Rd for a five-minute InBody scan. Your coach uses it to adjust your grams, so the plan moves with you.' Sample card (labelled 'Sample'): Week 0 → Week 4: weight 78.0 → 76.4 kg · body fat 36.1% → 35.0% · skeletal muscle 25.2 → 25.3 kg, small line chart. 'What the coach changed: calories stay at 1,610, protein stays at 140 g, Thursday's Beef Flank Steak becomes Haddock Loin to keep fat in range.' Button 'Book a scan'."
            },
            {
              "name": "Instagram",
              "purpose": "Show the DM channel",
              "content": "H2 'Already on Instagram? So is the Butler.' Sub 'DM PLAN to @jwfoods. Same coach, same numbers. When your week is ready, you get a link that opens here.' Phone mock on night navy, button 'Play the DM demo'. Script: user 'PLAN' → coach \"Hi! I'm the J&W Meal Butler coach, an AI. Lucas and Tasia check anything personal. What's the goal: lose fat, build muscle, maintain, or eating well on a GLP-1?\" → user 'lose fat. 86 kg, 6 ft, 35, gym 4x a week' → coach 'Got it. About 2,270 calories and 155 g of protein a day (estimate). Lunch and dinner, or the full day?' → user 'lunch and dinner. no fish pls' → coach 'Done: 10 meals, no fish, about 55 g of protein each. $139 a week on the Personal Macro Plan (Plus), or about $105 à la carte in our standard sizes.' → button 'Open my week'."
            },
            {
              "name": "Who it's for",
              "purpose": "Relatable use cases without fake reviews",
              "content": "H2 'Built for real weeks.' Persona cards labelled 'Sample people, not reviews': 'Early-shift nurse, Scarborough: lunch and dinner sized for 12-hour shifts, Saturday pickup after her scan.' · 'Lifter, Vaughan: Performance size on the Friday route.' · \"On a GLP-1, Ajax: smaller plates, more protein per bite, extra greens. Her prescriber stays in the loop.\" · \"Dad of three, Mississauga: his own plan rides on the family's Wednesday order.\""
            },
            {
              "name": "FAQ and talk to a person",
              "purpose": "Trust and human fallback",
              "content": "H2 'Questions, answered.' Accordion: 'Is the coach a real person?' → 'The coach is an AI that knows our menu, prices and delivery routes. A person at J&W approves every Personal Macro Plan and every weekly change before it reaches you. Medical questions always go to a person.' / 'How accurate are the macros?' → \"They're estimates built from our recipes, cooked weights and Health Canada's nutrient file, reviewed by a registered dietitian (concept). We lab-test our top sellers. Each portion is weighed, so the grams on your label are real.\" / 'Can I use it on a GLP-1 medication?' → \"Yes. The coach plans smaller portions with more protein and fibre. Keep your prescriber involved; we don't change medical advice.\" / \"What if I don't like something?\" → 'Tell the coach. It swaps like for like and shows you the price and macro change before you agree.' / 'Can I skip a week?' → 'Yes. Skip or pause any week before the Sunday cut-off. No contract, no cancellation fee.' / 'How does delivery work?' → 'Your plan comes frozen on your usual J&W route day at the normal route fee, or pick it up free at 2201 Brimley Rd.' / 'What happens to my data?' → 'We keep your answers to plan your food and nothing else. We never use your weight or health details for ads. Delete them any time.' Side card 'Rather talk to a person?' with initials avatars L (Lucas), T (Tasia), RD (partner dietitian): button 'Book a free 15-minute call'."
            },
            {
              "name": "Closing band",
              "purpose": "Final CTA",
              "content": "'Ready when you are.' Buttons 'Start my plan' and 'Chat with the Butler'. Framework dock follows."
            }
          ],
          "customerFlows": [
