        "prototype": {
          "concept": "A fundraising front door J&W does not have today. Organizers see what their group earns, work out a goal in two taps, and get a team page that an AI agent drafts in seconds. Parents and supporters use a real-feeling team page for the fictional Scarborough Snowhawks U11 AA: a scoreboard progress bar, the group's share under every price, a player picker, and checkout on J&W's real routes with a free team drop. The JW team view shows the December 2026 pilot: live campaigns, agent drafts to approve, the drop sheet, production and route impact, payouts, and the new customers the program brings in.",
          "wow": "On the Snowhawks team page a parent picks 'Maya R. #14' and taps Add on the Team Freezer Pack. The sticky bar shows '$20.10 to the Snowhawks' and a striped pending segment appears on top of the $456.12 already raised. After the demo checkout the segment fills in, the total counts up to $476.22, orders tick from 22 to 23, Maya's shout-out goes from 3 to 4 orders, and a thank-you card says exactly what this order sent to the team.",
          "design": {
            "inspiredBy": "Halenda's Fundraising (halendasfundraising.com): white utility bar with an outlined CTA pill, full-bleed photo hero with a dark overlay and centred white headline, short coloured rules under centred section titles, a light-blue two-way profit calculator card, a plain tier table, a numbered order block, an objection-handling FAQ and segment stories, with Raleway headings and Playfair serif accents. J&W's version adds what Halenda's lacks: per-team pages with a scoreboard progress bar, the share under every price (Rowe Farms idea), per-player links, one storefront with current prices, and rink and pitch line drawings in place of team photos. No Halenda's text, logos or photos.",
            "palette": [
              {
                "hex": "#154D8E",
                "role": "J&W laurel navy: links, secondary buttons, headings on light, progress 'raised' fill"
              },
              {
                "hex": "#0E1E36",
