            ],
            "displayFont": "Big Shoulders Display",
            "bodyFont": "Inter",
            "layout": "Mobile-first single column, 16px gutters, max width 1120px. Fonts: https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Big+Shoulders+Display:wght@700;800&family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap (Big Shoulders Display uppercase for headings and scoreboard numerals, Instrument Serif italic for one accent line per section, Inter body with tabular numbers in money). White utility bar under the concept bar: J&W logo ../assets/img/jw-logo.jpg (36px) + 'TEAM FUEL' wordmark and an outlined ember pill 'Start a fundraiser'. Centred section titles with a 40px ember rule. Hero: full-bleed chicken-burger photo under a rink-night gradient, centred headline; the 'at a glance' card overlaps the hero bottom on mobile and sits right of the headline on desktop. Team page: rink-night scoreboard band (crest circle with initials, big numerals, 14px progress bar with gold goal tick, sky rink-line SVG behind), pack cards 1 column on mobile, 2 on tablet, 4 on desktop; add-ons in a horizontal snap rail with the next card peeking. Sticky bottom bar on mobile while the team page is in view (items, total, share, 'Review order'), 52px, above the framework dock. Tables become stacked cards under 640px. Tap targets 44px. No horizontal scroll at 375px.",
            "tone": "Warm, local and practical, written for volunteer parents who are short on time. Short sentences, Canadian spelling, plain numbers, no hype, no pile-up of exclamation marks. A family butcher talking to a hockey parent at the rink."
          },
          "sections": [
            {
              "name": "S0 Season strip",
              "purpose": "Create timely urgency for the December pilot",
              "content": "Ember-tint strip, ember-deep text: 'Holiday freezer fundraiser: sign up by Sun Nov 22. Orders close Sun Dec 6, and your drop is the week of Dec 7.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "S1 Utility bar",
              "purpose": "Brand and the main action, Halenda's-style outlined CTA",
              "content": "J&W laurel logo + 'TEAM FUEL' wordmark. Links: How it works · Team page · Earnings · FAQ. Outlined ember pill button: 'Start a fundraiser' (scrolls to #start)."
            },
            {
              "name": "S2 Hero",
              "purpose": "Say the offer in one line and remove the three big objections",
              "content": "Background: chicken-burgers-1 image (https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1156/0176/files/chicken-burger-on-cutting-board.png?v=1782841639&width=1600) under a rink-night gradient. Eyebrow: 'J&W Team Fuel Fundraiser'. H1: 'Raise money with food your families already buy.' Accent line (Instrument Serif italic, sky): 'For teams, schools and clubs across the GTA.' Sub: 'Ontario chicken, butcher-cut beef and Meal Butler cooked meals from our family plant in Scarborough. Your group's share shows under every price. Nothing to pre-buy, no cash to collect, and one drop at your arena, field or hall.' Buttons: 'Start a fundraiser' (ember) · 'See a team page' (white outline, scrolls to #team). 'At a glance' card: '12% to 20% of every order goes to your group' · 'About $21 on a typical $135 order (est.)' · '$0 up front. Families pay J&W online' · 'One drop on our route day, or free pickup at 2201 Brimley Rd' · 'Paid within 10 business days of the drop' · 'Free \"Fuel for Game Day\" talk at $1,500 in sales'."
            },
            {
              "name": "S3 Proof band",
              "purpose": "Trust for schools, clubs and parents",
              "content": "Four items with simple line icons: 'Family butcher since 1995' · 'Ontario-inspected plant since 2008' · '4.8★ from 611 Google reviews' · 'Weekly routes from Port Perry to Hamilton'."
            },
            {
              "name": "S4 How it works",
              "purpose": "Halenda's numbered order block, rebuilt for an online team page",
              "content": "H2 'How it works', accent 'Four steps, about three weeks.' 1. 'Tell us about your group.' 'Name, goal, dates and where you practise. Your team page is ready within one business day.' 2. 'Share your link.' 'Every player or family gets their own link, so you can see who sold what. Post it in your team app, text it, or print the QR flyer.' 3. 'Families order online.' 'Supporters pay J&W directly. You never handle cash or product. Your group's share shows under every price.' 4. 'One drop, then you get paid.' 'We bring every order, bagged and labelled by name, to your arena or hall on our route day. Your group's money arrives by e-transfer or cheque within 10 business days.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "S5 Team page demo (the wow)",
              "purpose": "Show exactly what a supporter sees and let them order end to end",
              "content": "id 'team'. H2 'This is your team page', sub 'Here's what a family sees when they tap your link. Try it: add a pack and watch the bar move.' Grey tag 'Sample team. Names are fictional.' Scoreboard band (rink night): crest circle 'SH' · 'SCARBOROUGH SNOWHAWKS U11 AA' · 'Raising $750 for tournament fees and ice time.' · big numerals '$456.12' + 'raised of $750' · progress bar 61% with gold goal tick · '22 orders · 6 days left · Orders close Sun Dec 6' · drop chip 'Team drop: Wed Dec 9, 5:00–6:30 pm · team arena, east lot' · turf chips '✓ Coach talk unlocked' '✓ Raffle box unlocked' · pace chip 'On pace for about $705'. 'Who are you ordering for?' radio chips: Maya R. #14 · Ethan K. #7 · Arjun P. #22 · Leo M. #3 · Sofia D. #11 · Noah T. #9 · Just the team (default). Pack cards (photo, name, tags, pitch, contents, price, share chip '$X to the Snowhawks', stepper + Add): (1) Team Freezer Pack · 'Concept bundle' · 'About 23 lb of Ontario chicken and beef for the freezer.' · Premium Chicken Burgers, 25 × 6 oz ($35.50) / Case of Portioned Chicken Breast, 4 kg, 6 oz pieces, about 23 ($92) / Ground Beef Bulk Mix, 5 lb ($40) · $167.50 · $20.10. (2) Game-Week Meal Pack · 'Meal Butler' (slate) + 'Concept bundle' · '10 cooked meals and 2 egg-bite breakfasts for a week of practices and games. About 37 g protein per meal (est.). Heat in the bag.' · 3 Teriyaki Chicken, Green Beans & Rice / 3 Tenders, Broccoli & Sweet Potato / 2 Jerk Chicken, Green Beans & Sweet Potato / 2 Turkey, Spinach & Rice (all 4 oz) / 2 Egg White Bites, Spinach & Feta · $122.40 · $24.48. (3) Kids Favourite Combo · 'J&W box' · 'Weeknight dinners kids ask for.' · 4 chicken breasts 6–8 oz, 2 packs beef hot dogs, 2 × 1 lb ground beef, 1 lb cooked beef meatballs, 1 lb AAA beef stew, 2 kg breaded chicken fingers · $95.00 · $11.40. (4) Long Weekend Box · 'J&W box' · 'Steaks, ribs, sausages, burgers and sliders for a team barbecue.' · note 'Includes pork' · $199.00 · $23.88. 'Add to any order' snap rail with share chips: Beef Chili 10 oz $12 ($2.40) · Lemon Chicken Rice Soup $8.99 ($1.80) · Egg White Bites, Spinach & Feta $5.25 ($1.05) · Breakfast Wrap, Egg, Spinach & Feta $5.99 ($1.20) · Chicken Souvlaki Wrap $5.99 ($1.20) · Marinated Chicken Breast Case 4 kg, Korean BBQ $100 ($12.00) · AAA New York Striploin, case of 8 × 8–9 oz $110 ($13.20) · No-Salt Chicken Souvlaki Case 5 kg $95 ($11.40). Shout-outs: 'Ethan K. #7 · 4 orders' · 'Maya R. #14 · 3 orders' · 'Arjun P. #22 · 3 orders' + 'Families can hide their name.' Share row: 'Share this page' · Copy link · Text · Team app (toast 'Link copied (demo)'). Sticky bar when cart has items: '{n} items · {total} · {share} to the Snowhawks · Review order'. Extra real products from jw-catalog.json, defined locally: chicken-burgers-1 'Premium Chicken Burgers — 25 Pack (6 oz each)' $35.50 img https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1156/0176/files/chicken-burger-on-cutting-board.png?v=1782841639&width=600; ground-beef-10lb-bulk-mix-special 'GROUND BEEF - BULK MIX SPECIAL - 5lb' (show as 'Ground Beef Bulk Mix, 5 lb') $40.00 img https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1156/0176/products/GROUNDPORK.jpg?v=1613490076&width=600."
            },
            {
              "name": "S6 What your group earns + goal calculator",
              "purpose": "Halenda's tier table and two-way calculator, in J&W's honest numbers",
              "content": "id 'earn'. H2 'What your group earns', accent 'Same prices as our store.' Copy: 'Families pay our regular prices. J&W pays your group a share of every order from our side, and we show the exact amount under each price.' Rate table: 'Meal Butler cooked and portioned packs' 20% · 'Butcher boxes, freezer packs and cases' 12% · 'Orders through your team link for 6 months after the drop' 5%. Chip: 'Typical order $135 → about $21 for your group (est.)'. Fine print: 'Rates are a Concept for the 2026–27 pilot.' Sky-tint calculator card 'Goal calculator', two tabs. Tab 'I have a goal': Goal ($, default 1,000), Families (default 16) → 'About 48 orders. That's 3 per family: your own freezer fill plus two supporters.' (orders = ceil(goal / 21.06); per family = orders / families, 1 decimal; if ≤ 3.5 say 'your own order plus a couple of supporters', else 'about {n} per family') + button 'Start with this goal'. Tab 'I know our orders': Orders (default 40) → 'About $5,400 in sales and $842 for your group.' + '✓ Coach talk at $1,500 in sales' and '✓ Raffle box at $3,000 in sales' (grey if not reached). Footnote: 'Based on a $135 average order and a 15.6% average share. Estimates, not a promise.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "S7 Perks",
              "purpose": "Low-cost extras that help groups raise more and bring J&W into the team",
              "content": "H2 'A little extra for your team'. Card 1 'Fuel for Game Day': 'Pass $1,500 in sales and a J&W butcher brings a free 30-minute talk and a tasting tray to one practice. Early-ice breakfasts, tournament coolers, reheating at the hotel. General food tips, not medical advice.' Button 'Book your talk'. Card 2 'Raffle box': 'Pass $3,000 in sales and we add a Long Weekend Box ($199) for your team raffle or year-end barbecue.' Card 3 'Keep fuelling the team': 'For six months after your drop, every order through your team link still sends 5% to your group.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "S8 Who it's for",
              "purpose": "Segment entry points with the right season, like Halenda's segment stories",
              "content": "Six cards, each with a 'Plan a fundraiser' button that scrolls to #start with Type preselected: 'Hockey and ringette' · best Oct–Feb · 'Tournament fees, ice time, team jackets.' / 'Soccer and baseball' · best Mar–Jun · 'Spring kit, field rentals, travel.' / 'Schools and parent councils' · best Nov–Dec and Apr–May · 'Trips, playgrounds, graduation.' / 'Cadets, scouts and guides' · any time · 'Camps and gear.' / 'Dance, gymnastics and martial arts' · best Jan–Apr · 'Competition and recital costs.' / 'Faith and community groups' · any time · 'Youth programs and community meals.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "S9 Questions organizers ask",
              "purpose": "Objection handling before a principal or club board says yes",
              "content": "id 'faq', accordion. 'Do we have to pre-buy anything?' 'No. Families pay J&W online when they order. You never hold cash or product.' / 'When do we get paid?' 'Within 10 business days of your drop, by e-transfer or cheque, with a statement of every order.' / 'Is this a donation? Do buyers get tax receipts?' 'No. Your group's share is a fundraising payment from J&W, not a charitable donation, so we don't issue tax receipts.' / 'Can you deliver to our school?' 'School boards have their own fundraising and food rules. We send your principal a one-page school pack. Until your board says yes to a school drop, families can pick up free at Brimley Rd or choose home delivery.' / 'What if a family misses the drop?' 'We take their order back to Brimley Rd frozen and hold it 3 days for free pickup (Mon–Fri 9–6, Sat 10–4).' / 'Allergies, pork and halal?' 'Every pack comes with an ingredient and allergen sheet before your campaign starts, and our coordinator confirms anything specific. The Freezer Pack, Game-Week Pack and Kids Combo list no pork. The Long Weekend Box includes sausages and ribs. We don't label packs halal or kosher.' / 'Can relatives outside Ontario help?' 'Yes, if the food stays here. We deliver only in Ontario because our plant is provincially inspected. A grandparent in BC can buy a pack for a team family to pick up at the drop.' / 'How long should a campaign run?' 'Two weeks works well: open on a Monday, close on a Sunday, drop the next week on our route day.' / 'Where do you do team drops?' 'On our weekly routes: Tuesday in Durham (Pickering to Port Perry), Wednesday in Toronto, Scarborough, North York, Etobicoke and Mississauga, Thursday from Oakville to Hamilton, Friday in York and Peel. Farther away, families choose home delivery on our long routes.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "S10 Coming next: Team Fuel Jerky",
              "purpose": "Show the hand-sell idea honestly as in development and capture interest",
              "content": "Dashed card, tag 'Concept · in development'. H3 'Team Fuel Jerky'. 'We're working on a J&W-made jerky that players could sell by hand. It isn't for sale yet. It needs a tested recipe, shelf-life testing and approval under our provincial licence.' Email input (label 'Email') + button 'Tell me when it's ready'. 'Demo: nothing is sent.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "S11 Start a fundraiser",
              "purpose": "Organizer sign-up with an AI-drafted team page and share kit",
              "content": "id 'start'. H2 'Start a fundraiser', sub 'About two minutes. Our coordinator checks every page before it goes live.' Fields: Group name · Type (6 types from S8 + Other) · City (JWC.cities()) · Campaign window radio 'Holiday 2026 · Nov 23 – Dec 6' / 'Winter 2027 · Jan 18 – 31' / 'Spring 2027 · Apr 19 – May 2' · Goal ($) · Number of families · Drop spot ('Arena, field, hall or studio') · Your name · Email. 'Use sample' link: Rouge Valley Rapids U12 Girls · Soccer and baseball · Pickering · Spring 2027 · $1,000 · 16 · 'Soccer fields, north lot' · Dana L. · dana@example.com. 'Demo: nothing is sent.' Button 'Build my team page' → 900 ms shimmer 'Team Page Builder is drafting…' → draft card with slate badge 'Drafted by Team Page Builder': 'Your page: jwfoods.com/team/rouge-valley-rapids-u12 (demo)' · 'Goal $1,000 ≈ 48 orders, about 3 per family (est. at $21 an order).' · 'Orders open Mon Apr 19 and close Sun May 2, 2027. Drop: Tue May 4 on our GTA 1 route, 4:30–6:00 pm at Soccer fields, north lot. We'll confirm the spot with you.' · 'Perks: free coach talk at $1,500 in sales; raffle box at $3,000.' Share-kit tabs: Team app 'Rapids families: our J&W fundraiser opens Monday. Fill your freezer with Ontario chicken and beef, or grab a week of cooked Meal Butler meals. About $20 of every order goes to our team. One pickup at the field on Tue May 4. Order here: {link}' / Text 'Hi! Our soccer team is raising money with J&W Foods in Scarborough. If you buy meat or meal prep anyway, about $20 of your order goes to the team. Order by Sun May 2: {link}' / Email subject 'Help the Rapids and stock your freezer' / Flyer (QR placeholder SVG, team name, dates). Buttons 'Send for approval' · 'Edit'. Drop-day logic: first route from JWC.routesFor(city) that is not pickup or express; drop = that weekday in the week after close (Holiday Dec 8/9/10/11, 2026; Winter Feb 2/3/4/5, 2027; Spring May 4/5/6/7, 2027). Long routes ($35) show: 'Team drops run on our GTA routes. For {city}, families can choose home delivery on the {day} route, or we can plan a group drop for 40+ orders.'"
            },
            {
              "name": "S12 Closing band",
              "purpose": "Final call to action",
              "content": "Rink-night band. H2 'Ready when your team is.' 'Tell us your goal and your dates. We'll have your team page ready within one business day.' Buttons 'Start a fundraiser' (ember) · 'Call (416) 298-1350' (tel: link)."
            }
          ],
          "customerFlows": [
            {
              "name": "Parent orders a freezer pack for the team drop",
