    "million": {
      "intro": "A better website, with reviews, email and SMS flows, SEO and a modern store, could add roughly $150-400K a year on J&W's estimated $2.5M of sales. Getting to $1M of new revenue means changing what J&W sells (standing orders, gifts, workplace and clinical programs) and who it sells to (employers, gyms, clinics, schools). It can do that with the Ontario-inspected plant, the cooked line and the weekly routes it already has. Below are 11 ideas, each graded honestly, and a three-idea path that reaches about $1.3M a year by 2028 in the mid case.",
      "ideas": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "name": "Goal Plan Subscriptions",
          "short": "Quiz-led goal plans on a skip-anytime standing order",
          "idea": "Turn the Meal Butler cart customers rebuild every week into six goal plans sold weekly, every two weeks or as a monthly Freezer Fill, with 10% off for subscribing.",
          "how": "A 60-second quiz (goal, weight, training days, dislikes, GLP-1 use) picks one of six plans built only from about 31 current Meal Butler SKUs and shows estimated weekly macros and price per meal. Customers skip, pause or swap until the Sunday cut-off, and a Butcher's Pick default ships if they do nothing. Household boxes put everyone's plan in one delivery for one route fee. Launch to existing buyers and the 30K Instagram followers in December, then a New Year 6-Week Reset push.",
          "math": "Year 2: ~299 average active subscribers x $125 box x 26 deliveries x 0.9 (skips) = $875K + 240 one-off plan boxes x $135 = $32K = $907K gross x 0.8 incrementality = ~$726K (play-01.md, churn 10% in year 1 and 9% in year 2). Low ~$371K (25 adds a month, 12% churn), high ~$1.17M (45 adds a month, 8% churn; needs a second packing shift). Year 1 mid ~$341K. Gross profit at 40% = ~$290K; ~$170K contribution after ~$120K running costs.",
          "sales": {
            "low": 371000,
            "mid": 726000,
            "high": 1174000
          },
          "keepPct": 40,
          "takes": "About $7K setup (nutritionist review $2.5K, lab analysis of 8 SKUs $1.6K, photos, plan labels, staff training) plus about $7,450 a month in year 1: subscription app, Klaviyo share, ~$15K of ads at ~$85 CAC, a plan lead 12 h/week and a part-time cook/packer from February. No new licence.",
          "firstTest": "December pre-sale to existing buyers: three plans on Shopify subscriptions, a $25 switch credit and a Sunday cut-off. Pass if 60+ subscribers join in 30 days and 85%+ take a second delivery.",
          "worth": "The single best idea: it turns carts J&W already sells into recurring revenue at 40% margin, and every other play can feed it.",
