        "title": "Gifts now, Plans in December, Offices in January",
        "summary": "Start the Corporate Gift Studio this month. It is the only cash available in Q4 2026, it costs about $5.5K to start, and it puts J&W in front of HR teams and office managers. Launch Goal Plan subscriptions in December and push them in January: this is the highest-scoring idea, at 40% margin, on meals J&W already cooks. Pilot J&W at Work in January, when wellness budgets reset, with the employers met through gifting. The three mid cases add up to $1.72M a year by year 2. We count 75% of that, about $1.29M: roughly 5% of customers and orders overlap, and we take a further 20% off because one kitchen, one route fleet and one owner-led team carry all three launches at once. At about 40% margin that is roughly $516K of gross profit a year. If At Work stalls by June 2027, the B2B effort moves to the Pro Partner portal (idea 2) on the same routes. If Goal Plans run behind, the Clinical program (idea 10) is added as a referral channel. Plant and packing capacity must be confirmed before the January push.",
