      "rules": [
        {
          "q": "What exactly does J&W's provincial meat plant licence (Ontario Meat Regulation, O. Reg. 31/05 under the Food Safety and Quality Act) allow: co-branded partner labels, resale through gyms, grocers and fridges, gift deliveries, and a new cured or dried protein stick?",
          "why": "A provincial licence limits meat products to sale inside Ontario. Gifts, partner freezers and retail all depend on label and process rules being right, and a new dried or cured product needs a validated process before it is sold.",
          "who": "OMAFA meat inspection program and J&W's assigned inspector; OMAFA Agricultural Information Contact Centre"
        },
        {
          "q": "Does J&W hold any federal SFCR licence (for example for imports under its chicken quota), and what would it take to process meat for sale outside Ontario?",
          "why": "CFIA requires a federal licence to process meat for interprovincial trade or export. The Instagram 'CFIA Approved' claim must match what J&W actually holds. It gates national shipping, out-of-province gifts and some chain listings.",
          "who": "CFIA (My CFIA portal, local Ontario office) and an SFCR food-safety consultant"
        },
        {
          "q": "Which Meal Butler SKUs need a Nutrition Facts table and the front-of-package 'high in' symbol when sold away from the store, and which claims ('high protein', 'low sodium', 'GLP-1', 'heart-healthy') are allowed?",
          "why": "The front-of-package nutrition symbol has been mandatory for most prepackaged foods since Jan 1 2026. Freezer, partner, grocery and fridge sales lose the at-the-store setting, and nutrient-content and health claims are regulated.",
          "who": "Health Canada labelling guidance and the CFIA Industry Labelling Tool; a labelling consultant; a registered dietitian for clinical wording; the College of Dietitians of Ontario on referral and conflict-of-interest rules"
        },
        {
          "q": "When an employer pays for staff meals, what is taxable for the employee? Does a Pick-a-Box certificate count as a non-cash gift under CRA's $500 policy?",
          "why": "CRA allows $500 a year of non-cash gifts tax-free. A gift card or certificate is non-cash only if it is usable at identified retailers and cannot be converted to cash; otherwise it is taxable near-cash (CRA page dated 2026-07-27). Subsidised meals can be a taxable benefit depending on what staff pay. J&W supplies records, not tax advice.",
          "who": "CRA business enquiries; each client's payroll provider or accountant; J&W's own accountant"
        },
        {
          "q": "Can Team Fuel buyers get a charitable receipt? Who reports the group's share, how is HST handled, and do school boards allow product fundraisers?",
          "why": "Buying a product at full value is generally not a gift, so a receipt is not usually possible, and families will ask. The group's share is a payment from J&W, not a J&W donation. Schools follow board fundraising rules and Ontario's School Food and Beverage Policy.",
          "who": "CRA Charities Directorate; each school board's fundraising office; the club treasurer; J&W's accountant"
        },
        {
          "q": "Does a smart fridge or loaned freezer in an office, condo, gym or hospital need a public-health notice, inspection or business licence?",
          "why": "Unattended food sales are a food premises question under Ontario's Food Premises Regulation, enforced by each health unit (Toronto, Peel, York, Durham, Halton). Temperature logs and written site consent are needed.",
          "who": "Toronto Public Health and the other regional health units; City of Toronto Municipal Licensing & Standards; each site's property manager"
        },
        {
          "q": "What do marketplace, retailer and partner contracts commit J&W to: commission, price parity, slotting fees, payment terms, chargebacks and recall costs?",
          "why": "Uber Eats takes 20-30% on delivery and DoorDash 20-29%, often with price-parity terms. Grocers add slotting and promo costs. Loaned-freezer agreements need loss, return and termination terms.",
          "who": "J&W's lawyer; each retailer's category buyer; Uber Eats and DoorDash merchant terms"
        },
        {
          "q": "Is J&W insured for product liability at higher volumes, product recall, loaned equipment at partner sites and more route runs, and does it have a written recall and traceability plan?",
          "why": "Retailers and big employers ask for certificates naming them as additional insured. One recall at grocery or office scale could cost more than a year of profit from a play. Goodfood's 2026 CFIA licence suspension shows the risk is real.",
          "who": "J&W's commercial insurance broker; the OMAFA inspector (recall plan and records); CFIA recall guidance"
        }
      ]
    },
