            "milestone": "Goal Plans live in December and Butcher Club boxes from Dec 1. Every Sunday cut-off becomes Monday's cook, cut and pack sheet without manual tallying. Partner drops start in December and At Work pilots in January through the Business Desk."
          },
          {
            "name": "Scale routes, money and reach",
            "when": "Months 4-6 · Feb-Apr 2027",
            "agents": [
              "route-planner",
              "receivables-desk",
              "phone-line",
              "ads-analyst",
              "carcass-balancer"
            ],
            "milestone": "Routes planned in under an hour a day, net-15 invoices and reminders automatic once partners pass 4 paid orders, Sunday calls answered, ad spend moved weekly by town, and the first beef quarters on the yield log."
          },
          {
            "name": "Run it from one page",
            "when": "Months 7-9 · May-Jul 2027",
            "agents": [
              "monday-brief"
            ],
            "milestone": "Bill and Steven approve the week from a Monday Brief. Every agent is re-tuned on J&W's own data, holdout tests are read, and the year-2 calls are made: second packing shift, extra van, next plays."
          }
        ],
        "guardrails": [
          "People approve. Agents draft; a named person approves every price change, refund, credit, payout, new account, label, campaign and purchase order. Every approval is logged, and the Monday Brief shows what was approved, edited or rejected.",
          "Food facts come only from J&W's approved data. Macros and allergens are signed off by the partner dietitian and never come from the model's general knowledge. Medical, medication, pregnancy, eating-disorder and under-18 signals go to a person within one business day.",
          "No health or disease claims. Nothing about GLP-1, diabetes, \"salt and sugar free\" or \"no hormones\" goes live until the labelling consultant approves it. Meat orders and addresses are checked against the Ontario-only rule for a provincially inspected plant.",
          "CASL on every commercial message: express consent on file, sender ID and STOP in every text. J&W never messages fundraiser families or business contacts without consent or a valid exemption.",
          "Agents never handle card numbers or send money. They send payment links and draft invoices and payouts; the bookkeeper and owners release them. Discounts, save offers and ad budgets have hard caps.",
          "Honest and private. Real food in every photo (AI touches backgrounds only), no fake or undisclosed incentivized reviews, every AI reply labelled with a way to reach a person, and customer data kept in Shopify, Klaviyo and J&W's own sheets. Results are measured with holdouts, not vendor claims."
        ],
        "cost": {
          "text": "Once all 16 are live, the agents cost an estimated $1,600-3,500 a month in software, SMS and Claude API tokens (CAD; US-priced tools at about $1.37). Claude tokens are the small part, about $250-600 a month across every agent; the bigger lines are Klaviyo, the subscription app, SMS, Clay, Routific and the voice line. At year-2 volume, about 5,000 conversations a month and 1,000 orders a week, it rises to about $3,000-5,000 a month. That is less than one added full-time person (about $4,000 a month loaded) for desk capacity worth several. It excludes ad spend, lab tests, label stock, freezers and Minastech's fee, and many of these lines already sit in each play's cost table, so they should not be counted twice."
        }
      },
