    "skeptic": {
      "plays": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "year1": {
            "low": 171000,
            "mid": 341000,
            "high": 568000
          },
          "runRate": 726000,
          "marginPct": 40,
          "changed": true,
          "reason": "Arithmetic was correct, but churn was too low. It is now 10% a month in year 1 (was 9%) and 9% in year 2 (was 8.5%). 9% is the floor of the 8-15% meal-kit band, and J&W has never run a subscription. F&B subscriptions average 12-18% churn, and 44% of cancellations come in the first 90 days (market-benchmarks.md s5a). Year 1 falls about $9K and year 2 about $31K. Contribution is ~$47K in year 1 and ~$170K in year 2.",
          "mathYear1": "Subscribers ramp from 0 (Nov 2026 build month) to about 239 by Oct 2027. New subscribers: Dec 25, Jan 60, Feb 45, Mar 35, Apr 35, May 30, Jun 25, Jul 25, Aug 30, Sep 40, Oct 40 = 390, with 10% monthly churn. That gives 1,626 subscriber-months (avg 136 active) x $243.75 a month ($125 box after 10% off x 26 deliveries x 0.9 not skipped / 12) = $396K. Add 220 one-off plan boxes x $135 = $30K. Gross $426K x 0.8 incrementality = ~$341K added revenue (mid). Low: 245 new, 13% churn, $120 box, 12% skipped, 113 one-offs at $125, x0.75 = ~$171K. High: 555 new, 8% churn, $130 box, 325 one-offs at $140, x0.85 = ~$568K.",
          "mathRunRate": "Year 2 (Nov 2027-Oct 2028): start with ~239 active, add 35 a month, churn 9%. Average ~299 active x $2,925 a year ($125 x 26 x 0.9) = $875K, plus 240 one-off boxes x $135 = $32K. Gross $907K x 0.8 incrementality = ~$726K a year added revenue. Low ~$371K (25 adds a month, 12% churn); high ~$1.17M (45 adds a month, 8% churn; needs a second packing shift)."
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "year1": {
            "low": 81000,
            "mid": 179000,
            "high": 339000
          },
          "runRate": 581000,
          "marginPct": 22,
          "changed": true,
          "reason": "Three fixes. (1) Year 1 counted 4.33 order weeks a month (52 a year), but year 2 counts 50 ordering weeks. Year 1 now uses 4.17. (2) The year-1 average order is $240, not $260. Most account-months come from accounts under six months old, and the play says new accounts start near $180. (3) Incrementality is 0.80, not 0.85. The play's own pitch says gyms and trainers 'already send people to J&W', so gym freezers partly replace direct orders (at 22% margin instead of 45%). They also sell to the same fitness buyers Plays 1 and 6 count. Year-1 contribution is now about -$26K ($39K gross profit against ~$65K costs, including $18K of freezers). Year 2 is about +$50K.",
          "mathYear1": "November 2026 is the build and first drops go out in December 2026. Active accounts, net of ~2.5%/month churn, ramp 4 (Dec), 8, 12, 16, 19, 22, 24, 26, 28, 31, 34 (Oct 2027) = 224 account-months x 4.17 ordering weeks a month (50 a year, same as year 2) = 933 account-weeks x $240 average weekly order (young accounts start near $180, freezer accounts reach $400+) = $224,000 gross x 0.80 incremental = ~$179,200 net new revenue (mid). Gross profit at 22% = ~$39,400. Low: 124 account-months x 4.17 x $210 x 0.75 = ~$81,400. High: 330 account-months x 4.17 x $290 x 0.85 = ~$338,900.",
          "mathRunRate": "Year 2 (Nov 2027-Oct 2028): accounts grow from 34 to ~52, so 44 average active x $330/week x 50 weeks = $726,000 gross x 0.80 incremental = ~$580,800 net new revenue, with gross profit at 22% = ~$127,800. Range: low 30 x $280 x 50 x 0.75 = $315,000; high 55 x $380 x 50 x 0.80 = $836,000. Against J&W's own year-2 costs of ~$78,000, contribution is about +$50,000 before plant fixed-cost absorption and member-code DTC sales."
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "year1": {
            "low": 169000,
            "mid": 322000,
            "high": 484000
          },
          "runRate": 612000,
          "marginPct": 30,
          "changed": false,
          "reason": "Arithmetic reproduces: 1,772 member-months, 1,683 boxes, $429.6K gross, $322K; year 2 $612K; low and high check out. Incrementality is already at the 0.75 floor. 11% churn and 0.95 boxes a month give ~8.6 lifetime boxes, which matches truLOCAL's ~8 orders. The $235 AOV matches truLOCAL's ~$240. Wild Fork switchers are correctly inside the joins. Method note: boxes are counted on end-of-month members (joining = buying the first box), while Play 1 uses a mid-month average. On Play 1's method this play would be ~$301K, so treat $322K as the top of the mid range.",
          "mathYear1": "Members ramp 0->247 from Dec 2026 (Nov = build + waitlist): 415 joins (55 Dec, then 30-40/mo), 11% monthly churn -> 1,772 member-months x 0.95 boxes = 1,683 boxes x $235 avg order ($220 box + $15 add-ons) = $395.5K; + shares $34.0K (30 x 1/16 at $325 + 15 x 1/8 at $625 + 8 x 1/4 at $1,200 + 8 whole lamb at $475 + 6 half lamb at $250) = $429.6K gross x 0.75 incremental = $322K new revenue (low $169K: 249 joins, 13% churn, $215 AOV; high $484K: 540 joins, 9.5% churn, $245 AOV, 0.80 incremental)",
          "mathRunRate": "Year 2: 36 joins/month at 11% churn -> average 287 active members (steady state ~327) x 0.95 boxes x 12 = 3,268 boxes x $235 = $768.0K + shares $47.6K (1.4 x year 1) = $815.6K gross x 0.75 incremental = $612K a year (low $305K, high $957K)"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "year1": {
            "low": 68000,
            "mid": 162000,
            "high": 323000
          },
          "runRate": 622000,
          "marginPct": 40,
          "changed": false,
          "reason": "Arithmetic reproduces: 96 account-months, 30 freezer-months, $190,860 gross, $162K. Year 2 is $732,300 gross and $622K. Low and high check out. Inputs sit inside the model ranges. Watch points, not changed: (1) the mid case's 25% weekly participation equals the pilot's pass mark, so the mid assumes the pilot passes; (2) staff need somewhere at work to keep a week of frozen meals; (3) Team Table packs are modelled at $150, while the published packs are $115.80-$147.88 (about $133). That last one is immaterial (about -$0.6K in year 1), but the text should match.",
          "mathYear1": "Live from Jan 2027 (month 3). Team orders: accounts ramp 3 to 16 from Jan to Oct (3,4,6,8,10,11,12,12,14,16 = 96 account-months) x 4 order weeks x 40 items a week (new accounts start at about half the steady 55) x $10.00 average net item = $153,600. Freezers: 1 to 6 from Mar (30 freezer-months) x 4.2 weeks x $250 a week = $31,500. Team Table packs: 96 x 0.4 a month x $150 = $5,760. Gross $190,860 x 0.85 incrementality = $162K (mid). Low: 57 account-months x 4 x 30 items x $10 + 12 freezer-months x 4.2 x $200 + packs $1,710 = $80,190 x 0.85 = $68K. High: 145 account-months x 4 x 50 x $10.50 + 50 freezer-months x 4.2 x $300 + packs $11,963 = $379,463 x 0.85 = $323K.",
          "mathRunRate": "Year 2 (Nov 2027-Oct 2028): 22 average live accounts (16 rising to about 28) x 55 items a week x $10.00 x 48 weeks = $580,800, plus 9 freezers x $300 a week x 50 weeks = $135,000, plus 22 accounts x 5 packs x $150 = $16,500. Gross $732,300 x 0.85 incrementality = about $622K a year."
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "year1": {
            "low": 50000,
            "mid": 95000,
            "high": 232000
          },
          "runRate": 315000,
          "marginPct": 38,
          "changed": true,
          "reason": "Five trims. (1) Holiday 2026 is 18 accounts, not 25. The studio goes live Nov 9, and the first test's pass mark is 10+ companies and 200+ gifts by Nov 30. 25 accounts was 2.5 times that. (2) Occasion accounts fall from 25 to 20, because most come from holiday buyers. (3) Year-1 incrementality is 0.80, not 0.85. The play says first-season buyers are mostly existing J&W customers, and J&W already sells gift boxes. (4) Holiday 2027 is 60 accounts, not 70, because there are fewer first-season accounts to keep. (5) Margin is 38%, not 40%. The play's own note says volume tiers cut the 40% list margin, and the $120 average is already net of tiers. Year-1 contribution is now about break-even. Its year-1 value is Q4 cash and the door to HR buyers.",
          "mathYear1": "Holiday 2026 sprint (lean launch Nov 9): 18 accounts x 20 gifts x $120 = $43,200. Realtor and broker closings (from Jan, 0 to 35 agents): avg 15 active x 10 months x 1.2 gifts x $95 = $17,100. Occasion campaigns, Lunar New Year to Thanksgiving: 20 accounts x 15 gifts x $110 = $33,000. Milestone certificates from Mar: 8 accounts x 3 gifts x 8 months x $100 = $19,200. Follow-on orders: 1,032 gifts x 60% new x 8% x $130 = $6,440. Gross $118,940 x 0.80 incrementality = ~$95K (mid), about 45% in Nov-Dec 2026. Low: 10 holiday accounts x 18 x $115, 10 agents, 12 occasion accounts, 5 milestone accounts, 5% follow-on, x0.75 = ~$50K. High: 35 x 25 x $125 holiday, 25 agents at 1.4 gifts x $100, 35 occasion accounts x 18 x $115, 12 milestone accounts x 4 gifts, 10% follow-on, x0.85 = ~$232K.",
          "mathRunRate": "Year 2: Holiday 2027, 60 accounts (about 13 retained at 70% + 47 new) x 24 gifts x $122 = $175,680 + closings 40 agents x 12 months x 1.2 x $95 = $54,720 + occasions 40 accounts x 15 x $110 = $66,000 + milestones 15 accounts x 3 x 12 x $100 = $54,000 + follow-on 3,156 gifts x 60% x 8% x $130 = $19,690 = $370,090 gross x 0.85 = ~$315K. Low ~$140K (40 holiday accounts x 20 gifts); high ~$500K (90 holiday accounts x 26 gifts). Gross profit at 38% = ~$120K."
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "year1": {
            "low": 113000,
            "mid": 191000,
            "high": 276000
          },
          "runRate": 417000,
          "marginPct": 45,
          "changed": false,
          "reason": "Arithmetic reproduces: 380 client-months x 4.33 x 0.77 = 1,267 paid weeks x $170 x 0.70 = $150.8K. Carts are 1,045 x $33 = $34.5K and scans 230 x $25 = $5.8K, for $191K in total; year 2 is $417K. The 0.70 net factor already removes existing-customer spend and the PMP clients who would have joined Play 1. The remaining overlap with Play 1 (same front door, audience and January push, about 20% of this play) is taken in the portfolio discount, so the standalone figure is unchanged. Text to fix: play-01 says coach-led subscribers count in Play 6, but play-06 says coach standing orders count in Play 1. Rule: a fixed-plan standing order is Play 1, and a Personal Macro Plan is Play 6.",
          "mathYear1": "Launch Jan 4 2027 (month 3) after a 10-client December pilot. Personal Macro Plan: 380 client-months (12 in Jan rising to 57 in Oct) x 4.33 weeks x 0.77 active = 1,267 paid weeks x $170 = $215,383 gross x 0.70 net factor (existing-customer spend and Play 1 overlap removed) = $150,768. Coach-built one-time carts: 1,045 x $33 incremental = $34,485. Walk-in scans: 230 x $25 = $5,750. Total ~$191K (mid). Low: 760 paid weeks x $160 x 0.70 = $85,140 + 70% of carts and scans ($24,140 + $4,025) = ~$113K. High: 1,774 paid weeks x $180 x 0.70 = $223,491 + 130% of carts and scans ($44,830 + $7,475) = ~$276K.",
          "mathRunRate": "Year 2: PMP 70 enrolled on average (60 rising to 80) x 52 weeks x 0.77 active x $170 = $476,476 gross x 0.70 = $333,533; coach-built carts 180 a month x 12 x $33 = $71,280; walk-in scans 40 a month x 12 x $25 = $12,000. Total ~$417K a year (low ~$299K at 50 clients; high ~$535K at 90 clients)."
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "year1": {
            "low": 46000,
            "mid": 129000,
            "high": 271000
          },
          "runRate": 308000,
          "marginPct": 20,
          "changed": false,
          "reason": "Arithmetic reproduces: 42 campaigns x 25 orders x $135 = $141,750 x 0.80 = $113,400, plus follow-on $18.1K x 0.85 = $15.4K, gives $129K. Year 2: 85 campaigns gives $253.4K + $54.7K = $308K. Incrementality of 0.80 and 0.85 and the 20% margin after the group share and displacement are consistent with model-assumptions.md. The figures are left as they are, but the play is out of the year-1 plan. Its margin is thin, year 1 is break-even, it clashes with Gift Studio deliveries in December, and schools need board approval.",
          "mathYear1": "Campaigns by drop month: Dec 4, Jan 3, Feb 4, Mar 5, Apr 6, May 6, Jun 3, Jul 1, Aug 1, Sep 4, Oct 5 = 42 campaigns (about 38 groups) x 25 orders x $135 = $141,750 x 0.80 incremental = $113,400. Follow-on: 1,050 orders x 0.9 unique x 70% new = 662 new households x 12% repeat = 79 x 4 orders a year x $130 x 5.26/12 months left = $18,100 x 0.85 = $15,385. Year 1 mid ~$129K. Low: 25 campaigns x 18 orders x $125 x 0.75 = $42,188 + follow-on $3,803 = ~$46K. High: 60 campaigns x 32 orders x $140 x 0.85 = $228,480 + follow-on $42,638 = ~$271K.",
          "mathRunRate": "Year 2: ~85 campaigns (27 returning groups x 1.5 + 45 new) x 27 orders x $138 = $316,710 x 0.80 = $253,368. Follow-on: year-1 cohort 79 households x 60% still active x 4 x $130 = $24,767, plus year-2 cohort 1,343 new households x 12% = 161 x 4 x $130 x 5.67/12 = $39,589; together x 0.85 = $54,702. Run-rate ~$308K. Gross profit after the group share and displacement ~$62K (20%)."
        }
