        "note": "The path still clears $1M, but with less room. Corrected mid cases: Goal Plans $726K + At Work $622K + Gift Studio $315K = $1.66M (was $1.72M). The 25% discount is kept: 5% double counting is right for these three, because gifts count only in Play 5 and office staff who subscribe at home count only in Play 1, plus a 20% stretch. That gives ~$1.25M a year in year 2 (was $1.29M) and ~$494K gross profit at a ~39.6% blend (was $516K). The path reaches about $1.0M of annualised run-rate only at the end of 2027 ($1.00M at Q4 2027, helped by Holiday 2027 gifts in the trailing 12 months) and is clearly above it from Q1 2028 ($1.14M). Revenue actually banked in year 1 is only ~$0.45M ((341+162+95) x 0.75), so the page must not imply $1M in the first twelve months. The low cases give ~$0.62M and the high cases ~$2.0M. How the ramp is built: Goal Plans = quarter-end active (142, 184, 221, then 265, 296, 319, 336, 349) x $2,925 + $32K one-offs, x 0.8. At Work = accounts 6, 11, 14, 18, 21, 24, 27, 30 at 40 items in 2027 and 50-55 in 2028, x $10 x 48 weeks, plus freezers and packs, x 0.85. Gifts = trailing 12 months of the corrected Play 5. Label the ramp as annualised run-rate, not quarterly revenue, and say that gifts use a trailing basis. The original Q3 2027 At Work value ($324K) was high for 14 accounts at 40 items; the play's own inputs give ~$290K. Condition: by year 2 the path adds ~3,100 cooked items a week, against the ~2,000 that first test 2 checks for, so a second shift has to be costed before the January push."
      },
      "issues": [
        "The seven plays as written sum to $1.49M in year 1 and $3.67M in year 2 before overlap (+60% and +147% on a ~$2.5M business with 10-18 staff). After corrections they sum to $1.42M and $3.58M. Present the five-play plan (1, 3, 4, 5, 6) with a 28% overlap: ~$0.80M in year 1 and ~$1.94M in year 2.",
        "Play 1 and Play 6 contradict each other. play-01.md s2.4: 'Subscribers who come in through the coach chat are counted in Play 6 only.' play-06.md s2: 'Standing orders created from the coach (Subscribe & Save) are counted in Play 1.' Neither counts them, but the pages must agree: a fixed-plan standing order is Play 1, a Personal Macro Plan is Play 6.",
        "Play 1: 9%/8.5% monthly churn is the floor of the meal-kit band for a first-ever subscription. Now 10%/9%: year 1 $341K (was $350K), year 2 $726K (was $757K).",
        "Play 2: year 1 counted 52 order weeks while year 2 counts 50. The year-1 $260 average order ignores young accounts starting near $180. The 0.85 incrementality ignores the play's own 'already send people to J&W'. Now $179K in year 1 and $581K in year 2, and year-1 contribution is about -$26K.",
        "Play 5: the Holiday 2026 assumption (25 accounts, 500 gifts) is 2.5 times its own first-test pass mark. Year-1 incrementality of 0.85 conflicts with 'mostly existing customers', and the 40% margin conflicts with its own volume-tier note. Now $95K in year 1 and $315K in year 2 at 38%; year-1 contribution is about break-even.",
        "Idea 7 in million.md came from selection.json (0.95 incrementality, $300K, 17% keep) and was never synced to play-07.md (0.80, $308K, 20%). Remove the s9 note once it is updated.",
        "Ideas 7, 8 and 9 used incrementality of 0.90-0.95, above the mandatory 0.75-0.85. million.md's definition line '(0.75-0.95)' contradicts model-assumptions.md and should read 0.75-0.85.",
        "Idea 9 assumes $450 a week per fridge, but Play 4 uses $250-300 for the same frozen menu. Corrected to $350; payback goes from ~1.7 to ~2.6 years per ~$9K unit.",
        "Idea 10 removed overlap with idea 1's GLP-1 Companion only, not with Play 2's clinic partners or Play 6's GLP-1 users. The factor is now 0.70 and the mid ~$311K.",
        "Risk scores were generous for ideas 4 (18 to 16), 6 (19 to 16), 7 (18 to 17) and 10 (17 to 14). Fit was low for idea 3 (15 to 17). Re-scored totals: 1=86, 3=78, 4=75, 2=74, 5=70, 6=63, 7=63, 10=59, 8=52, 9=46, 11=33. Butcher Club is now second, so the $1M page needs one line on why it is not in the path (30% margin) but is in the year-1 plan.",
        "Path: $1.72M becomes $1.66M, $1.29M becomes ~$1.25M, and $516K gross profit becomes ~$494K. 'Crosses $1.0M in Q4 2027' should read 'reaches about $1.0M at the end of 2027'. Add that year-1 path revenue is only ~$0.45M and the low case is ~$0.62M.",
        "The path ramp mixes annualised run-rates (Plans, At Work) with trailing 12 months (Gifts). Label it as annualised run-rate, not revenue banked in the quarter.",
        "Capacity is not costed. By year 2 the five-play plan adds ~4,100 cooked items and ~300 delivery stops a week; today J&W runs an estimated 60-160 delivery orders a week. A supervised second shift, cold storage and probably a second reefer van ($1.8-2.6K a month lease) sit outside the plays' costs, roughly $60-100K a year beyond their own labour lines. Confirm with first test 2 before the January push.",
        "People: Lucas or Tasia are named as lead on Plays 1, 2, 4, 5, 6 and 7 (roughly 35-65 hours a week combined at peak). Budget a growth or operations coordinator, or the 20% stretch discount is too small.",
        "Headcount is inconsistent: model-assumptions.md says ~15-25 staff, while jw-audit.md says 10-18 today. Client pages should say 'about 15 people' or '10 to 18'.",
        "Play 3 counts boxes on end-of-month members, while Play 1 uses a mid-month average. That is acceptable (joining = first box), but on Play 1's method Play 3 year 1 would be ~$301K, so $322K is the top of the mid range.",
        "Play 4: the mid case assumes the pilot's 25% weekly participation pass mark is met, and it does not say where staff keep a week of frozen meals at work. Team Table packs are modelled at $150, while the published packs are $115.80-$147.88 (immaterial, about -$0.6K in year 1).",
        "Plays 1 and 6 together assume ~1,800 goal-led quiz or coach interactions a month from one 30K-follower audience. Run them as one front door with one funnel KPI. The residual overlap (~20% of Play 6) is in the portfolio discount.",
        "Gift Studio and Team Fuel collide in December (pilot drops Dec 1 and 7, gift peak the week of Dec 14), share the outreach desk and both claim follow-on orders from new households. Team Fuel's repeat buyers may be the same households Plays 1 and 3 count as joins. Keep Team Fuel out of year 1.",
        "Pro Partner and At Work both loan freezers, share the B2B prospecting agent and account lead, and can land the same clinic or hospital (as can idea 9). Run them in sequence: At Work first, Pro Partner only if At Work stalls by June 2027.",
        "Idea 11's mid is a once-licensed run-rate. With a 12-24 month licence timeline, little of it falls inside year 2; say so on the page.",
