    "edited": {
      "hub": {
        "title": "Seven ways to turn Scarborough's 4.8-star butcher|into the GTA's protein brand",
        "intro": "Bill, Stavros: you already have what most meal-prep brands lack, from your own Ontario-inspected plant and 30 years of butchery to 4.8 stars from 611 Google reviews. What is missing is the packaging around it: standing orders, business buyers and a website that shows what your customers already say. Below are seven working prototypes, each modelled on a business that proves the idea, with numbers checked line by line and a plan that starts with three.",
        "compIntro": "Each prototype borrows from one business that already makes the idea pay: four in the GTA or Canada and three abroad. We took the mechanics, not the words or the design, and checked every one on October 16, 2026."
      },
      "realFacts": [
        "Family butchers since 1995. J&W was founded by Stavros Trougakos and William (Bill) Fehr, carrying on a trade that began with George Trougakos's downtown Toronto butcher and grocery in the 1960s and Advance Food Products in 1973.",
        "An Ontario-inspected meat plant since 2008, at 2201 Brimley Rd, Scarborough. J&W also holds a 2026 federal chicken import quota as a processor.",
        "979 products online at jwfoods.com (743 available on Oct 16, 2026), including about 292 cooked and portioned Meal Butler items, all salt and sugar free with no added oils.",
        "4.8 stars from 611 Google reviews, up from 295 in early 2023, and 30K followers on Instagram.",
        "Weekly delivery routes: Durham on Tuesday; Toronto, Scarborough, North York, East York, Etobicoke and Mississauga on Wednesday; Oakville to Hamilton on Thursday; York and Peel on Friday ($20 to $27). Long-haul runs reach places like Peterborough, London, Windsor and Ottawa ($35). $100 minimum, order by Sunday, free pickup in Scarborough.",
        "Express delivery in 1 to 2 business days for $30 ($100 minimum) in Scarborough, North York, Toronto, East York, Etobicoke, Richmond Hill, Markham and Vaughan.",
        "Every price in the prototypes is J&W's own published price on Oct 16, 2026, for example cooked chicken breast at about $4.20 to $4.99 for 4oz, pre-set meals at $8.99 to $18.39 and the AAA ribeye 10-pack at $175. New items are labelled Concept.",
        "Product photos are J&W's own, from jwfoods.com. Macros shown are estimates, because J&W does not publish nutrition panels online."
      ],
      "baseline": {
        "low": 1200000,
        "mid": 2500000,
        "high": 4000000,
        "confidence": "Low",
        "note": "No reported figure exists, so we triangulated D&B's modelled $1.07M, ZoomInfo's under-$5M ceiling, ISED labour-cost ratios for a 10-to-18-person butcher and processor, and a build-up of routes, store and wholesale."
      },
      "fee": {
        "monthly": 3500,
        "setup": 6000,
        "term": "6-month first term, then month to month, with a day-90 KPI review",
        "includes": "Placeholder for Erwin to confirm. Set at the bottom of our range because year 1 is a build year. Covers: building the five year-one plays on J&W's Shopify from the prototypes (Gift Studio, Goal Plans, Butcher Club, At Work portal, AI Coach); setting up the 10 core AI agents in the first 90 days and the 6 add-ons in months 4 to 9, each with written approval rules; Klaviyo flows, the reviews app, GA4 and catalogue clean-up; running the first tests against their pass marks; a Monday report and a monthly review with Bill and Stavros; training the J&W team. Not included: J&W's own costs in each play (food, staff hours, freezers, totes, ad spend, app subscriptions, dietitian and lab fees)."
      },
