          "pricing": "Signature meals US$12.20–$19.20 (about C$17–27). Meal plans US$11.39–$14.09 a meal, 5% Subscribe & Save. Cooked chicken by the pound US$15.20 (about C$21.58). Custom bowls from US$6. No published wholesale price list.",
          "model": "Heat-and-eat meals sold direct and wholesale to stores, gyms, weight-loss clinics, training centres and offices, from a few dozen meals to thousands a week (company claim). Ships frozen on dry ice with an 8-meal minimum.",
          "scale": "Over US$14M revenue in 2023 with 75 staff (Garage Gym Reviews). 56% annualised growth from 2014 to 2021 (UFC). 12M+ meals sold (company claim). 157K Instagram followers.",
          "borrow": "The wholesale page order (proof, segments, plant story, a shoppable grid with macros and steppers), the audience router, a low per-order minimum and a coach's shared-cart link. Ideas only, no copy.",
          "jwEdge": "An Ontario-inspected plant with in-house butchery since 2008, family wholesale roots back to 1973 and a 2026 chicken TRQ processor quota. Cooked chicken at C$16.72–19.96/lb against C$21.58, and a comparable bowl at about C$10 against C$18.63. Food arrives frozen on J&W's own routes, not on dry ice. And J&W can ship what Icon never built: a working application, a tiered price list and net terms.",
