          "premium": "Named-farm Canadian meat with grass-fed and organic lines, flash-frozen and vacuum-sealed. The Ontario default for monthly meat delivery.",
          "pricing": "Starter $155 (up to 36 servings), Family $279 (up to 80), Mega $349 (up to 104). One-time curated boxes $170–$250 and value boxes $200–$305. Free shipping with no minimum. New members get one free item in every box.",
          "model": "Members spend a points budget on cuts, can buy extra points, get a reminder 48 hours before billing, and skip, pause or cancel online. A free-meat-for-life hook, a comparison table against grocery and other boxes, and a corporate gifting funnel round it out.",
          "scale": "70,100+ customers and 511,000+ boxes since 2016 (company claim). About $19.8M revenue in 2020, then acquired by EMERGE Commerce for up to $16.8M. 2025 AOV about $240, CLTV approaching $2,000, CAC $100–175. Trustpilot 3.2 from 68 reviews.",
          "borrow": "Serving-sized tiers, the points builder, the 48-hour reminder, a free item in every box, and $/lb with a compare table.",
          "jwEdge": "J&W cuts, portions and seals in its own Ontario-inspected plant. AAA ribeye is about $23–25/lb in the 10-pack against $39–60/lb at Toronto premium butchers, and J&W offers Wagyu, bison, venison, Ontario lamb and cut-to-thickness steaks truLOCAL does not. It delivers on its own weekly routes instead of by courier, has a cooked Meal Butler pack to use as the free item, and holds 4.8 stars from 611 Google reviews.",
