          "premium": "Chef-led ready meals, fresh and never frozen, 15 new dishes a week, and 4.8 on Trustpilot from 6,584 reviews.",
          "pricing": "Consumer plans $11.99–$15.49 a meal with a 6-meal minimum; premium dishes add $1.95–$4.25. Workplace meals about $11.75 (CEO, Aug 2025). Employers fund anywhere from $1 a meal to 100%.",
          "model": "The employer sets an allowance and invites staff by company email. Staff pick meals each week, and everything rolls into one office order that cancels itself if nobody orders. The invoice splits company and employee shares, the price per meal falls with company volume, and larger firms get on-site fridges.",
          "scale": "About 90,000 meals a week and nearly 400 staff (Retail Insider, Aug 2025). 150,000+ customers (company claim). Now delivers in Quebec, Ontario, the Maritimes and Western Canada. Revenue about $60M a year (estimate).",
          "borrow": "Allowance types and caps, domain-locked invites, the weekly joint order, the split invoice and volume-tiered pricing.",
          "jwEdge": "J&W's frozen, vacuum-sealed meals suit an unattended office freezer with no use-by waste. Its Scarborough plant and Tuesday to Friday routes already pass the Scarborough, Markham, North York, Vaughan and Mississauga business parks, while WeCook couriers from Quebec. Pre-set meals cost $9.99–13.99, at or below WeCook's, with no added salt, sugar or oil against 795–1,015 mg sodium in WeCook's sample bowl. And J&W can add a butcher range for the team barbecue.",
