        {
          "name": "Halenda's Fundraising",
          "url": "https://halendasfundraising.com/",
          "scope": "GTA (Durham Region)",
          "hq": "Oshawa, Ontario",
          "category": "Group fundraising",
          "premium": "Family-owned since 1979, with award-winning smoked meats (three Diamond Awards at Ontario's Finest Meat) and charcuterie in Metro, Sobeys, Foodland and Fortinos. It is value-priced, so it is the benchmark for the channel, not for positioning.",
          "pricing": "Pepperoni Stix: a case of 24 bags costs a group $261–$300 and sells at $25 a bag, so groups keep 50–56%. Shipping $18 a case anywhere in Ontario; pickup free in Oshawa or Etobicoke.",
          "model": "Groups either buy cases and then sell (about 95%) or collect orders first with a personalised flyer and then buy (about 5%). The site has a two-way profit calculator, a tier table, a sales-rep field, a school-compliance FAQ and success stories by segment.",
          "scale": "6 million+ meat sticks sold and more than $6M raised for groups since June 2013 (company claim). About 1,880 cases and $0.5M of wholesale revenue a year (estimate). Five Durham stores and two plants.",
          "borrow": "The profit calculator, the group's share shown in plain numbers, the school-compliance FAQ and success stories by segment.",
          "jwEdge": "Halenda's sells cases to the group, so supporters never become its customers. On a J&W team page each family buys direct, with consent, and becomes a J&W customer. Baskets are bigger and are food families already buy: a typical $135 order sends about $21 to the group against $12.50–$14.13 per $25 bag, with no upfront case purchase. J&W adds pork-free packs, cooked meals for sports weeks and a Tuesday Durham route past every Halenda's store. Halenda's stays ahead on track record, field reps and a shelf-stable hand-sell product.",
          "sources": [
