      ],
      "roi": {
        "intro": "This page puts a number on each prototype: what it could add in its first year and once it is running, what is left after the cost of the food, and what J&W's running costs and our fee take back. It opens on the five-play plan, with 28% taken off for overlap and for one small team running five launches. Year 1 is a build year, when gross profit roughly pays for the plays' own costs. Year 2 is where the return shows. Every figure is an estimate, so change any input to test it.",
        "adsMonthly": 500,
        "method": [
          {
            "t": "Added revenue",
            "d": "Each play counts only new sales. Orders J&W would have had anyway are removed with a factor of 0.75 to 0.85. Year 1 runs from November 2026 to October 2027 and includes the ramp. Year 2 is a full year once running."
          },
          {
            "t": "Three cases",
            "d": "Low, expected and high come from each play's own build: subscribers, accounts, gifts or members, times J&W's published prices. The expected case is the planning number. The low case is roughly what happens if each first test only just passes its mark."
          },
          {
            "t": "Overlap",
            "d": "The five plays share one audience (Instagram, the email list, the counter), one kitchen and one route fleet. We take 28% off: about 8% for customers counted twice and 20% for the stretch of five launches between November and January. The discount applies to sales and gross profit, not to costs."
          },
          {
            "t": "Margin",
            "d": "Gross margin by type, after food, packaging and card fees but before overheads: cooked meals 45%, subscriptions 40% after the 10% discount, gifts 38%, raw butcher boxes 30%, wholesale 22%, fundraisers 20% after the group's share. For comparison, Goodfood reported 41.7% in fiscal 2025."
          },
          {
            "t": "Cost and return",
            "d": "All-in cost is our fee and setup, the shared promotion budget, and each play's own setup and running costs (staff hours, freezers, totes, software and its own ads). With the default inputs, year-1 gross profit of about $302K sits below the all-in year-1 cost of about $376K, so year 1 is an investment. In year 2, gross profit of about $742K is roughly 1.8 to 2.3 times the cost; the lower figure uses each play's higher year-2 running costs. Our fee alone is earned back by about $111K of added sales at the blended margin."
          },
          {
            "t": "Promotion",
            "d": "Each play's costs already include its own paid ads. The $500 a month here is a shared brand budget for boosted Reels, the Google Business Profile and review requests. Raise it to test heavier spending."
          },
          {
            "t": "What is not counted",
            "d": "The lift on today's business from reviews, email, SMS and search clean-up (roughly $150K to $400K a year, estimate). Capacity beyond each play's own labour: a supervised second shift, cold storage and probably a second reefer van, about $60K to $100K a year from mid-2027. A hired growth or operations coordinator. Pro Partner and Team Fuel, which are backups and switched off by default."
          },
          {
            "t": "Sources",
            "d": "J&W prices come from jwfoods.com on October 16, 2026. The baseline comes from our audit (D&B, ZoomInfo, ISED). Margins, churn and acquisition costs come from shared assumptions built on Goodfood, Eightx, Klaviyo and Triple Whale benchmarks. Competitor proof comes from the seven deep-dives. A separate CFO pass re-ran every play's arithmetic."
          }
        ]
      },
