        "strengths": [
          "Its own Ontario-inspected plant since 2008, with butchery, cooking and portioning under one roof. No GTA meal-prep rival has one.",
          "Price leader on premium protein: AAA ribeye at about $23 to $25/lb against $31 to $60/lb at premium GTA butchers, and cooked chicken at about $1.05 to $1.25/oz against $1.86/oz at Hi Chef.",
          "A clean recipe promise across the cooked line: salt and sugar free, with no added oils.",
          "Frozen, vacuum-sealed portions keep for months, so one weekly route reaches Ottawa and Windsor and a monthly Freezer Fill is possible. Fresh rivals last 3 to 10 days.",
          "A strong, growing reputation: 4.8 stars from 611 Google reviews, and customers know Bill, Tasia and Lucas by name.",
          "A real audience and word of mouth: 30K Instagram followers, and reviews show trainers and gyms already send clients.",
          "Wholesale roots back to Advance Food Products (1973) and a 2026 federal chicken import quota as a processor.",
          "Raw and cooked in one cart, plus Wagyu, whole animals and about 154 Greek and Mediterranean specialties."
        ],
        "gaps": [
          "No subscription or auto-reorder, so regular customers rebuild the same cart every week.",
          "No reviews on the website. The 611 Google reviews never reach a product page.",
          "No page for gyms, employers or gift buyers: no application, tiered pricing or net terms, despite the wholesale history.",
          "No email or SMS platform and no Google Analytics. Only a native newsletter form and a Meta pixel.",
          "51% of products have empty or very short descriptions, 59 have no image and 413 have no product type. At least one gift box description contains pasted dictation text.",
          "No macros or nutrition panels on product cards, and no quiz, goal plans or coach.",
          "Close to invisible in search for 'meal prep Toronto' or 'butcher Scarborough'. The meta description is a list of hashtags.",
          "Listings disagree on hours, postal code and delivery minimum ($100 or $130), and Instagram says 'CFIA Approved' while the site says Ontario-inspected.",
          "One delivery day per zone, with no slots or tracking, while the GTA standard is Sunday and Wednesday.",
          "The brand rests on a few people in a team of about 10 to 18, and Facebook has been quiet since January 2024."
        ],
